WEBVTT

00:48.460 --> 00:51.980
Why is that?
Why is it three kilos lighter?!

00:51.980 --> 00:55.110
We changed the material
of the cockpit frame.

00:55.110 --> 00:57.570
It's stronger now.
No safety loss.

00:57.570 --> 01:00.790
I should hope not!
Who'd make it more dangerous?

01:00.790 --> 01:02.290
Why didn't you tell?

01:02.290 --> 01:04.710
Well, you wanted it
ten days sooner.

01:06.270 --> 01:08.810
Blame it on Char and his Neo Zeon.

01:08.810 --> 01:11.840
We wouldn't be rushing
through this...

01:11.840 --> 01:16.010
...if he hadn't decided to
drop an asteroid onto Earth.

01:17.940 --> 01:19.510
- This it?
- Yes.

01:26.190 --> 01:31.980
<b>[AnimeRG] Presents:</b>

01:26.190 --> 01:31.980
<b>MOBILE SUIT GUNDAM</b>

01:27.140 --> 01:31.980
CHAR'S COUNTERATTACK

01:45.720 --> 01:46.960
Come on!

01:52.310 --> 01:54.980
What are we accused of, anyway?!

01:54.980 --> 01:57.970
Kidnapping a minor
and evading arrest!

02:00.030 --> 02:03.640
You punks shouldn't be fooling
around here on Earth anyway.

02:03.640 --> 02:06.500
You're Quess Paraya,
aren't you?

02:06.500 --> 02:09.900
- How could you!
- Come on, Quess!

02:10.830 --> 02:14.300
Darling, she bit me!
Quess bit my hand!

02:14.300 --> 02:15.820
Did you, Quess?

02:15.820 --> 02:17.070
Take a look at this!

02:17.070 --> 02:18.610
- We'd better get going.
- I know, but...

02:18.610 --> 02:19.910
Come on.

02:22.380 --> 02:24.120
Have a safe trip...

02:24.120 --> 02:25.700
...Mr. Adenauer.

02:25.700 --> 02:27.550
What was that about?

02:27.550 --> 02:29.500
Just the family life of a top...

02:29.500 --> 02:31.670
...Earth Federation
government official.

02:31.670 --> 02:34.800
They figure she'll behave better
if they take her out into space.

02:34.800 --> 02:37.130
But that wasn't his wife, was it?

02:38.900 --> 02:41.640
Why can't we travel
on a military plane?

02:41.640 --> 02:43.430
The military's been mobilized.

02:43.430 --> 02:46.100
It's safer for us to take a
civilian flight from Hong Kong.

02:46.100 --> 02:48.730
Why couldn't you
stop Char's plans...

02:48.730 --> 02:50.900
...of putting earth in a deep-freeze?

02:50.900 --> 02:53.560
The Federation Government
didn't believe that...

02:53.560 --> 02:55.650
...Char Aznable was still alive.

02:55.650 --> 02:58.490
There are ten billion people
living in outer space.

02:58.490 --> 03:00.950
You think you really know them...

03:00.950 --> 03:02.740
...even though you're on Earth.

03:02.740 --> 03:05.080
That's harder to believe.

03:05.080 --> 03:06.950
Nevertheless...

03:17.770 --> 03:18.590
Where is it?!

03:18.590 --> 03:20.430
In direct line with the North Star!

03:20.430 --> 03:21.930
Give me the coordinates!

03:21.930 --> 03:23.970
It's no use! Pull back!

03:25.450 --> 03:30.430
Five, four, three,
two, one...

03:30.430 --> 03:31.690
Ignition!

03:37.710 --> 03:39.110
Lieutenant Amuro!

03:39.110 --> 03:41.990
Fifth is accelerating towards Earth!

03:46.630 --> 03:48.790
Entry angle of Fifth, check.

03:48.790 --> 03:50.540
Speed, check.

03:51.010 --> 03:53.170
Is Captain Char on
the mobile suit deck?

03:53.170 --> 03:54.830
Yes. He's in the Sazabi.

03:55.640 --> 03:59.300
Captain. Gyunei Guss'
unit is in a deadlock.

03:59.300 --> 04:01.670
I think we need to offer support.

04:01.670 --> 04:04.340
We've done what's required
to send Fifth Luna to Earth.

04:04.340 --> 04:06.490
Signal all units to withdraw.

04:06.490 --> 04:09.310
I have. But we're unable to
emit Minovsky particles...

04:09.310 --> 04:13.270
...to prevent them from
detecting our mobile suits.

04:13.270 --> 04:15.310
And that puts Gyunei in danger.

04:15.310 --> 04:16.730
Right.

04:18.290 --> 04:22.070
We'll back up Gyunei's
Jagd-Doga and bring him in!

04:23.420 --> 04:24.950
Sazabi cleared for takeoff!

04:24.950 --> 04:26.740
Launch!

04:55.870 --> 05:00.150
I can't believe we couldn't stop
this asteroid from crashing to Earth.

05:13.390 --> 05:15.080
More reinforcements.

05:15.080 --> 05:16.500
Char?!

05:19.440 --> 05:20.750
Captain!

05:24.690 --> 05:26.600
That was a mine.

05:26.600 --> 05:28.890
The Minovsky particles
have thinned out.

05:28.890 --> 05:31.350
Why are you crashing this to Earth!

05:31.350 --> 05:34.730
Temperatures will drop and
it'll become uninhabitable!

05:34.730 --> 05:36.270
It'll cause a nuclear winter!

05:36.270 --> 05:40.020
Those living on Earth
care only about themselves.

05:40.020 --> 05:42.400
That's why I've decided
to get rid of them all.

05:48.920 --> 05:51.620
You have no right to
punish them that way!

05:59.520 --> 06:03.250
It is Char Aznable's destiny
to enforce discipline, Amuro!

06:03.250 --> 06:04.340
You're full of yourself!

06:04.590 --> 06:07.300
I'm saying Earth isn't going to last.

06:08.940 --> 06:11.180
Not with that!

06:12.950 --> 06:16.310
Captain!
You're not using your funnels!

06:23.790 --> 06:26.280
Captain! Don't worry about me!

06:26.280 --> 06:28.240
Gyunei. You'll come with me.

06:28.240 --> 06:29.860
I can make it!

06:29.860 --> 06:32.870
No way.
Not the way you look.

06:32.870 --> 06:36.330
You did well protecting
the nuclear thrusters on Fifth.

06:55.490 --> 06:58.140
But this is a valid ticket.

06:58.140 --> 06:59.640
I'm sorry.

06:59.640 --> 07:01.020
Are you ready, sir?!

07:01.020 --> 07:03.440
Forget it.
There's no way I'm going with her.

07:03.440 --> 07:05.900
I'd rather freeze here on Earth.

07:05.900 --> 07:07.400
Good idea.

07:10.420 --> 07:11.990
I can't take this!

07:11.990 --> 07:12.990
Kathy...!

07:12.990 --> 07:14.700
- Come on. Let's go!
- Right...

07:15.380 --> 07:18.660
This is the letter from the
Federation government.

07:18.660 --> 07:20.500
All right. Make it two.

07:20.500 --> 07:22.580
Yes, sir. Two tickets.

07:29.190 --> 07:30.170
Mister.

07:30.170 --> 07:31.590
Yes?

07:33.690 --> 07:36.820
- Their letter of recommendation?
- Yes.

07:36.820 --> 07:40.020
From John Bauer of the
Federation government.

07:41.200 --> 07:42.740
Let one of them on board.

07:42.740 --> 07:43.400
Sir?

07:43.580 --> 07:46.520
We jumped the line
with my political privileges.

07:46.520 --> 07:49.230
Besides, I owe Bauer a favor.

07:50.170 --> 07:52.570
Politicians are all the same.

07:52.570 --> 07:54.870
Ma'am!
We can take one of you.

07:54.870 --> 07:57.080
I'll put two on the next shuttle?

07:57.080 --> 07:59.290
There might not
be a next shuttle.

07:59.290 --> 08:03.040
Well. According to the news,
war's broken out.

08:03.040 --> 08:04.810
Then I'm going to send him.

08:04.810 --> 08:06.460
Hathaway Noa.

08:06.460 --> 08:08.380
Destination is Londenion, right?

08:08.380 --> 08:09.210
Yes.

08:09.210 --> 08:12.050
His father's stationed there.
Hathaway.

08:13.110 --> 08:15.930
Here. The shuttle
will be departing soon.

08:15.930 --> 08:16.800
But, Mom...

08:16.800 --> 08:18.850
You're a big boy now.

08:18.850 --> 08:21.060
It's time you experienced space.

08:21.060 --> 08:22.600
What about you and Cheimin?

08:22.600 --> 08:23.810
We're okay.

08:23.810 --> 08:26.060
This war won't last very long.

08:26.060 --> 08:29.750
As this man says, we'll
catch up in no time.

08:29.750 --> 08:31.240
You sure?

08:31.240 --> 08:32.360
Of course.

08:38.130 --> 08:40.160
I'm taking the
Re-GZ for a checkup.

08:40.160 --> 08:42.370
- Thanks, Chief Hanan.
- Sir!

08:47.270 --> 08:50.250
Side 2 hasn't started
their attack yet?

08:50.250 --> 08:51.840
I know. They're slow.

08:51.840 --> 08:54.930
You think Side 1 wouldn't
assist the Londo-Bell unit?

08:55.800 --> 08:58.430
They're afraid their colonies
might rebel.

08:58.430 --> 09:00.200
It's here! A heat source!

09:00.200 --> 09:02.390
Side 2 has commenced
their laser attack.

09:02.650 --> 09:04.730
But there are too few of them.

09:04.730 --> 09:06.440
They can't destroy it
with that number.

09:06.440 --> 09:08.360
It's continuing its descent
toward Earth!

09:08.360 --> 09:11.780
Have they issued a warning
about Fifth Luna's descent?

09:11.780 --> 09:13.690
To those in Lhasa, Tibet?

09:13.690 --> 09:17.210
The people who have the
information probably fled.

09:17.210 --> 09:19.760
That's exactly why Char
has the upper hand.

09:19.760 --> 09:20.910
Anyway...

09:20.910 --> 09:23.830
...Char needed a lot of energy
to propel Fifth Luna.

09:23.830 --> 09:26.000
How did he get all
that nuclear power?

09:26.000 --> 09:28.330
The Federation government?

09:28.330 --> 09:30.000
Hard ascent now!

09:30.000 --> 09:31.840
Laser attack's letting up.

09:43.950 --> 09:45.670
Justice!

09:45.670 --> 09:48.230
Hail! Neo Zeon!

09:52.330 --> 09:54.440
We're clear for takeoff.

09:54.440 --> 09:55.360
But Vice-Minister...

09:55.360 --> 09:58.320
...we'll be coming close
to an asteroid.

09:58.320 --> 09:59.820
I'm well aware of that.

09:59.820 --> 10:02.910
As long as we get to
Londenion on time.

10:03.840 --> 10:05.790
- We'll wear our spacesuits.
- Right.

10:06.760 --> 10:07.920
Thank you.

10:07.920 --> 10:09.040
Sure.

10:31.710 --> 10:32.520
What's wrong?

10:32.520 --> 10:34.070
Look at that! A fireball!

10:34.070 --> 10:34.650
What?

10:34.650 --> 10:36.820
Captain! Steer us to the right!

10:36.820 --> 10:37.950
There it is.

10:37.950 --> 10:40.160
It's further north than I expected.

10:44.970 --> 10:47.080
You've got to go further right!

10:52.680 --> 10:54.800
Captain! Further to the right!

10:54.800 --> 10:56.250
Stay seated!

11:00.360 --> 11:03.090
Please. Don't let this happen...

11:36.730 --> 11:38.260
How pathetic.

11:38.260 --> 11:41.340
We can't do anything but
watch Char do as he wants.

11:41.340 --> 11:42.880
- I'm going to the moon!
- Amuro!

11:43.570 --> 11:44.720
Astonaige!

11:44.720 --> 11:46.180
Did you prepare the sled?!

11:46.180 --> 11:48.070
It's outside and ready to go!

11:48.070 --> 11:51.810
For two years now, all the
colonies have been inspected.

11:51.810 --> 11:55.560
But why couldn't we figure out
Char was putting together a force?!

11:55.560 --> 11:59.360
The Federation government
rules the space colonies from Earth.

11:59.360 --> 12:02.820
But there are a great many
Spacenoids who resent that.

12:02.820 --> 12:04.570
Every time we inspect them...

12:04.570 --> 12:07.490
...the general public will
help to hide the facts.

12:08.220 --> 12:09.950
There won't be a second wave.

12:09.950 --> 12:10.700
I'm heading out.

12:10.700 --> 12:15.080
If all goes well, I might defeat
Char before he gets to Sweetwater.

12:41.710 --> 12:45.660
Did you know Anaheim makes
mobile suits for Neo Zeon, too?

12:45.660 --> 12:46.570
You sure?

12:46.570 --> 12:47.990
Come on, give us a break.

12:47.990 --> 12:50.620
We in the technical division
have nothing to do with that.

12:50.620 --> 12:53.370
Just like a corporation.

12:58.850 --> 13:00.130
Mr. October...

13:00.130 --> 13:03.800
...wouldn't believe that I was a
crewmember on the Ra-Cailum!

13:03.800 --> 13:07.050
It's because you're just
way too cute, Chan.

13:07.690 --> 13:10.640
You'll find a psycommu
receiver pack behind the seat.

13:10.640 --> 13:12.430
Will the monitor work?

13:12.430 --> 13:13.890
Sure.

13:14.870 --> 13:16.440
Good.

13:16.440 --> 13:19.860
If the psycommu reads the
enemy's brainwaves better...

13:19.860 --> 13:21.880
...it'll speed up our reaction time.

13:21.880 --> 13:24.820
Lieutenant, we took
that idea of yours...

13:24.820 --> 13:27.780
...and our R & D division
developed the apparatus...

13:27.780 --> 13:30.950
...but built it right into the frame.

13:31.430 --> 13:33.750
- You built it right into the frame?
- Yes.

13:33.750 --> 13:37.830
These computer chips are
about the size of metal particles.

13:37.830 --> 13:39.460
They're integrated into the frame.

13:39.460 --> 13:41.380
That's a pretty good idea.

13:41.380 --> 13:44.460
And so we used it
for this cockpit frame.

13:45.610 --> 13:48.840
But you said you don't know
the specifics of this technology?

13:48.840 --> 13:51.390
Just the information from R & D.

13:51.390 --> 13:54.730
We'd like to test the frame
when we return to our unit.

13:54.730 --> 13:55.850
I understand.

13:55.850 --> 13:58.410
I'm taking Nu Gundam
back with me right now.

13:58.410 --> 14:00.900
We'll need three more days
to equip it for battle.

14:00.900 --> 14:02.070
Unacceptable.

14:02.070 --> 14:03.400
Not good enough.

14:03.400 --> 14:05.780
The operation to drop Fifth Luna...

14:05.780 --> 14:09.660
...marks the first major battle
of the Neo Zeon fleet.

14:09.660 --> 14:12.990
It has given me the opportunity
to observe you in action.

14:13.200 --> 14:14.750
I'm impressed.

14:14.750 --> 14:17.910
We conclude our mission today
with diversionary operations...

14:17.910 --> 14:20.750
...against the pursuing
Londo-Bell unit.

14:20.750 --> 14:22.710
It's a simple plan.

14:22.710 --> 14:26.130
I wish you success before our
triumphant return to Sweetwater.

14:26.130 --> 14:27.630
Thank you!

14:27.630 --> 14:29.230
That was first-rate.

14:29.230 --> 14:30.970
I feel like a total clown.

14:30.970 --> 14:34.430
As Neo Zeon leader you must
maintain your public image.

14:34.430 --> 14:36.020
Captain!

14:36.530 --> 14:39.270
I apologize for what
happened on Fifth Luna!

14:39.270 --> 14:42.110
We've cyber-enhanced you
at the Newtype Labs.

14:42.110 --> 14:45.360
It cost quite a lot.
We can't afford to lose you.

14:45.360 --> 14:47.440
Don't worry about it.
Get ready.

14:47.440 --> 14:48.450
Right!

14:48.450 --> 14:50.030
Newtype Labs Director...

14:50.030 --> 14:51.490
...I mean, Operations Officer!

14:51.670 --> 14:53.280
Lieutenant.

14:53.280 --> 14:55.240
Is Gyunei fit to go with us?

14:55.240 --> 14:57.410
He's a bit oversensitive, but...

14:57.410 --> 14:59.540
...his skills as a guard
are excellent.

14:59.540 --> 15:02.790
The scenery at the Colony
will calm him.

15:02.790 --> 15:04.670
Do you think his skills
are too enhanced?

15:04.670 --> 15:06.210
He's just young.

15:06.210 --> 15:07.460
Captain.

15:07.460 --> 15:08.720
Please understand...

15:08.720 --> 15:11.130
You are the leader of Neo Zeon.

15:11.130 --> 15:15.640
That's why I'm getting ready
to act like a politician.

15:15.640 --> 15:17.770
- Take care of the operation.
- Yes, Captain.

15:18.620 --> 15:20.270
The enemy is moving.

15:20.270 --> 15:21.830
What are they up to?

15:21.830 --> 15:24.360
And between the moon
and Side 1. That Char!

15:24.360 --> 15:26.150
What could they be thinking?

15:26.150 --> 15:29.280
Anaheim is likely to be
monitoring us.

15:29.280 --> 15:30.240
Get Amuro!

15:30.240 --> 15:31.340
Right!

15:31.340 --> 15:34.030
Combat bridge, get a move on!

15:42.220 --> 15:43.350
What is it?

15:43.350 --> 15:45.420
From the Ra-Cailum.

15:47.190 --> 15:50.410
Char's second wave is
close to the moon?

15:50.410 --> 15:53.280
They want me back
to Londo-Bell right away?

15:53.280 --> 15:55.350
The psycommu receiver
is fine for now.

15:55.350 --> 15:55.930
What?

15:55.930 --> 15:56.970
Are you going?

15:56.970 --> 15:58.390
But we're not done...

15:58.390 --> 15:59.270
Here it is.

15:59.270 --> 15:59.890
You going?!

15:59.890 --> 16:01.810
- I'll turn it on.
- It's impossible!

16:01.810 --> 16:03.140
There's got to be a way to do it.

16:03.350 --> 16:04.600
Amuro...

16:04.600 --> 16:06.300
Do it.

16:06.300 --> 16:07.820
Okay.

16:12.250 --> 16:14.490
Chan! The Booster Bed and...

16:14.490 --> 16:16.910
...the Mass Driver, right?!
- Right!

16:21.680 --> 16:23.580
What's this operation?

16:23.580 --> 16:26.730
I thought mobile suits were
designed for close combat.

16:26.730 --> 16:28.520
Get moving, Rezin!

16:28.520 --> 16:30.550
You'll do it your own way, anyway!

16:30.800 --> 16:32.920
Whatever...

16:43.730 --> 16:45.520
Please stop this!

16:45.080 --> 16:46.310
You won't make it in time!

16:46.310 --> 16:47.900
We're going.

16:49.500 --> 16:51.690
I warned you!

16:55.070 --> 16:58.450
Launch trajectory set!
SSE, standing by for orders!

16:58.450 --> 16:59.660
Looks good on you.

16:59.660 --> 17:01.660
Just part of my duty.

17:02.680 --> 17:04.750
Yes! SSE here!

17:04.750 --> 17:07.420
The mobile suits will
begin combat shortly.

17:07.420 --> 17:09.210
- That'll be your signal to launch.
- Roger!

17:09.850 --> 17:11.380
Any time now.

17:11.380 --> 17:12.130
Yes.

17:12.130 --> 17:14.610
Main bridge, watch for the signal.

17:14.610 --> 17:17.430
Countdown progressing!

17:18.900 --> 17:20.470
Mr. October!

17:20.470 --> 17:22.390
The psycommu frame sample!

17:22.390 --> 17:24.140
Send it to the Londo-Bell unit!

17:24.140 --> 17:26.600
I'll forward it! Zero!

17:40.720 --> 17:42.450
So, we still can't use the Re-GZ?

17:42.450 --> 17:44.250
It won't be repaired in time!

17:44.250 --> 17:45.580
I know that.

17:58.320 --> 18:01.010
Chan... Chan?

18:07.040 --> 18:08.730
Please come back.

18:19.130 --> 18:21.030
Keep firing! Three more seconds!

18:21.030 --> 18:23.530
All fleets, commence
evasive action!

18:24.470 --> 18:27.250
Now's our chance to squash a few.

18:50.500 --> 18:52.440
Found you.

18:53.330 --> 18:55.530
One of them got past
our mobile suit force!

18:55.530 --> 18:56.990
Counterattack! Barrage!

18:56.990 --> 18:58.110
Barrage!

19:07.300 --> 19:09.410
Close the bulkheads!
Fire team!

19:09.410 --> 19:13.500
The Moon and Earth.
Capella, Vega and the Sun.

19:13.750 --> 19:15.960
We must be right here.

19:15.960 --> 19:18.260
And the fleet...

19:18.260 --> 19:19.670
Hey, Chan.

19:20.860 --> 19:22.720
You okay?

19:22.720 --> 19:24.360
Sure.

19:24.360 --> 19:26.220
Where's the fleet?

19:27.160 --> 19:28.680
Has it started?

19:28.680 --> 19:29.640
Yeah.

19:30.200 --> 19:31.520
I'll get behind you.

19:31.520 --> 19:32.520
Thanks.

19:32.520 --> 19:36.190
See that?! Those lights over there!

19:40.750 --> 19:43.070
Change course!
There's a battle over there!

19:43.070 --> 19:44.320
Oh, right!

19:44.320 --> 19:47.580
Get the Apogee Motors fixed,
or we'll head straight into it!

19:47.580 --> 19:49.250
No way!

19:49.250 --> 19:51.580
Oh, god!

19:58.060 --> 19:59.630
I'm on it!

20:01.570 --> 20:03.930
Where are the Jegan teams?!

20:03.930 --> 20:06.140
The barrage is thinning out!

20:07.740 --> 20:09.140
That's Kayra's machine!

20:09.140 --> 20:11.140
Kayra! Do you read me?!

20:11.140 --> 20:12.770
You'll be hit with friendly fire!

20:12.770 --> 20:14.150
Get out!

20:15.310 --> 20:18.070
The Lieutenant's not here!

20:20.420 --> 20:23.490
Pretty good.
Though a bit messy.

20:37.140 --> 20:38.800
What?

20:40.520 --> 20:42.340
Reinforcements?

20:46.110 --> 20:47.600
There!

20:50.820 --> 20:53.020
That machine's not in the computer.

20:56.200 --> 20:57.650
Neo Zeon?!

20:57.650 --> 20:59.480
Take a look for yourself.

20:59.480 --> 21:00.820
Is it war?

21:00.820 --> 21:02.610
It looks like it.

21:03.550 --> 21:05.280
Signal to pull back!

21:10.930 --> 21:12.750
A Gundam!?

21:20.350 --> 21:22.000
- They're pulling back.
- What?

21:24.190 --> 21:25.720
Well organized.

21:25.720 --> 21:27.640
They knew when to withdraw.

21:28.110 --> 21:29.260
What's that ship!?

21:34.950 --> 21:36.980
Do not pass this point!

21:36.980 --> 21:38.860
Do not leave the officers' mess hall.

21:38.860 --> 21:42.150
Due to the lack of gravity,
please step firmly.

21:45.590 --> 21:46.740
Hathaway?

21:46.740 --> 21:48.450
Dad!

21:51.510 --> 21:53.290
Hey...

21:53.720 --> 21:55.660
So, you were on the shuttle.

21:55.660 --> 21:56.750
But why?

21:56.750 --> 21:59.500
I didn't know you were the
Captain of this ship...

21:59.500 --> 22:01.310
Where's your mom and Cheimin?

22:01.310 --> 22:04.170
Oh. They only let one of us
on the shuttle.

22:04.170 --> 22:05.700
Captain.

22:05.700 --> 22:08.470
I'm sorry to break up
your family reunion, but...

22:08.470 --> 22:11.760
Oh, he's the one who got me
on the shuttle.

22:11.760 --> 22:13.010
I see.

22:13.010 --> 22:14.430
You must be the Vice-Minister.

22:14.430 --> 22:15.350
Yes.

22:15.350 --> 22:17.640
You'll need to redirect
this ship to Londenion.

22:17.640 --> 22:19.650
I'm on a special mission.

22:19.650 --> 22:20.560
Hathaway...

22:20.560 --> 22:22.360
Go straight to the mess hall now.

22:22.360 --> 22:24.280
We'll discuss why
you've come later.

22:24.280 --> 22:24.940
Sure!

22:32.840 --> 22:34.910
Lalah Sune?

22:37.600 --> 22:41.960
Don't think you can keep both
Char and me for yourself!

22:41.960 --> 22:45.260
It would be torture if one's
consciousness lasted forever.

22:45.260 --> 22:47.590
But I'd still like to
watch over both of you.

22:47.590 --> 22:48.930
That's selfish!

22:48.930 --> 22:51.970
I want to remain with
both of you eternally.

22:52.140 --> 22:53.970
Forget about Char!

22:54.450 --> 22:56.810
Char is pure.

22:57.990 --> 22:59.980
Pure?!

23:01.450 --> 23:05.570
Darn. Starting to have
the same dreams again.

23:06.400 --> 23:07.880
Lieutenant.

23:07.880 --> 23:09.240
What is it?

23:09.240 --> 23:12.280
Could you come to
the mobile suit deck?

23:12.280 --> 23:13.660
- I'll be there in ten!
- Sure.

23:15.800 --> 23:18.790
What's wrong with him?
So cold suddenly.

23:36.950 --> 23:38.270
Chan.

23:43.200 --> 23:44.230
I got hit?

23:44.230 --> 23:47.190
That's what happened,
Quess Paraya.

23:49.420 --> 23:52.280
That's because the controls
aren't right for my hands!

23:52.280 --> 23:54.200
They'd be the right size
if you wore a pilot suit.

23:54.200 --> 23:56.490
Can I try it now?

23:56.490 --> 23:57.740
This is great.

23:57.740 --> 23:59.660
They've already come up
with a simulation...

23:59.870 --> 24:02.330
...using data from the last battle.

24:02.330 --> 24:06.590
It's a military secret.
Don't mention it to anyone.

24:08.170 --> 24:09.800
Hey.

24:10.860 --> 24:13.360
I think she's got good instincts.

24:13.360 --> 24:17.680
Well, I had no idea
she had any interest in this.

24:18.450 --> 24:22.140
Creepo. He's so two faced.

24:22.140 --> 24:23.350
Quess Paraya?

24:23.350 --> 24:24.480
Yes!

24:24.480 --> 24:27.110
I'd advise against civilians
going past this point.

24:27.110 --> 24:28.230
Oh, sorry.

24:28.230 --> 24:29.600
Quess!

24:29.600 --> 24:31.610
You'll get in the way.
Come back.

24:31.860 --> 24:33.780
Go on ahead!

24:33.780 --> 24:35.700
He just doesn't get it.

24:35.700 --> 24:38.370
Over here! Amuro!

24:39.930 --> 24:40.870
Here!

24:40.870 --> 24:43.290
Right. What's the problem?

24:43.290 --> 24:47.040
I see. So, that's Amuro Ray.

24:47.690 --> 24:50.050
"Over here!" huh?

24:50.050 --> 24:53.050
Quess! I shot down two enemies!

24:53.050 --> 24:56.050
Cool! That's how many I got!

24:59.070 --> 25:00.560
Didn't you feel anything?

25:00.560 --> 25:03.020
He seemed like any other grownup.

25:03.020 --> 25:03.560
Here.

25:03.560 --> 25:04.810
Thanks.

25:05.250 --> 25:06.190
Yeah, but...

25:06.190 --> 25:09.480
...everybody says he actually
knew how to pilot a mobile suit...

25:09.480 --> 25:12.880
...the first time he got in one
and wiped out a Zeon Zaku.

25:12.880 --> 25:14.380
Think it's true?

25:14.380 --> 25:16.160
Just by sitting in the cockpit...

25:16.160 --> 25:19.330
...he totally understood the
Gundam circuits and everything.

25:22.010 --> 25:23.780
What's so funny?

25:23.780 --> 25:26.330
That's what they call a Newtype.

25:26.330 --> 25:28.020
You're right.

25:28.020 --> 25:31.630
That's different from what
Christina of India told me.

25:31.630 --> 25:36.010
She says a Newtype psychically
comprehends people and things.

25:36.010 --> 25:38.800
She said no matter how far
away they may be...

25:38.800 --> 25:40.850
...they can figure these things out.

25:40.850 --> 25:41.840
Yeah.

25:41.840 --> 25:44.520
Back when humans
only lived on Earth...

25:44.520 --> 25:47.940
...they were only able to use
half their brain cells, right?

25:47.940 --> 25:49.480
But when they went into space...

25:49.480 --> 25:52.320
...people started to use
the other half.

25:52.320 --> 25:55.800
So, they improved their telepathy
and precognition abilities.

25:55.800 --> 25:58.870
Otherwise, families split up
between the space and Earth...

25:58.870 --> 26:01.490
...would lose their sense of family.

26:01.490 --> 26:04.660
Your family seems to
get along pretty well.

26:04.660 --> 26:07.500
But my dad still gets on my nerves.

26:07.500 --> 26:11.500
Our family's always lived on Earth.

26:40.170 --> 26:43.780
We're on target, thanks to
the code the Federation provided.

26:43.780 --> 26:45.870
They're pretty casual
with their information.

26:45.870 --> 26:48.370
No, Captain.

26:48.370 --> 26:50.670
It was thanks to our groundwork
behind the scenes.

26:50.670 --> 26:52.590
I know.

27:04.280 --> 27:07.350
So, that's the new mobile suit.

27:10.370 --> 27:12.870
This is off limits to civilians.

27:12.870 --> 27:15.230
They let me in here before.

27:15.920 --> 27:18.070
Anyway, what're you doing here?!

27:18.070 --> 27:20.050
What? What do you mean?

27:20.050 --> 27:23.120
I'm a mechanic on this ship.

27:23.120 --> 27:25.200
That's not what I meant.

27:25.200 --> 27:28.000
You grownups always give
the same kind of answer.

27:28.000 --> 27:29.620
What's your relationship
with Amuro?!

27:29.620 --> 27:31.430
Relationship?

27:31.430 --> 27:33.880
He's a senior officer who I respect.

27:33.880 --> 27:35.910
That's not what I mean.

27:35.910 --> 27:38.340
I studied in India.

27:38.340 --> 27:42.130
About how humanity can become
Newtypes and feel for each other.

27:42.130 --> 27:46.310
That's why I have an interest
in Amuro, who's a Newtype.

27:46.310 --> 27:48.560
So, why do you interfere?

27:48.560 --> 27:49.680
Interfere?

27:49.680 --> 27:51.890
That's the way I see it!

27:51.890 --> 27:53.560
Get off this ship now!

27:53.560 --> 27:56.580
I can't do such a thing?

27:56.580 --> 27:58.070
Well, then... Then, I'll...

27:58.070 --> 27:59.820
Quess!
You're not supposed to...!

27:59.820 --> 28:01.240
Get lost!

28:02.000 --> 28:03.110
Grab this!

28:03.110 --> 28:04.660
No!

28:11.640 --> 28:13.920
Quess! There's the Colony.

28:13.920 --> 28:15.000
Colony?!

28:15.000 --> 28:17.460
Side 1 's Londenion.

28:27.450 --> 28:29.680
There's a city inside a cylinder.

28:29.680 --> 28:31.390
With lakes, too.

28:31.390 --> 28:35.020
It makes me think
people really can evolve.

28:35.020 --> 28:38.230
I can see why the Zabis
fought for independence.

28:38.230 --> 28:40.780
But the Zabi Family's Zeon
lost to the Feddies, right?

28:40.780 --> 28:41.780
Yeah, but...

28:41.780 --> 28:43.860
My father knows nothing
about these colonies...

28:43.860 --> 28:46.870
...and yet rules them from Earth.

28:46.870 --> 28:50.540
Char was once on
the side of Earth...

28:50.540 --> 28:54.930
...but now he's totally bent
on destroying the planet.

28:54.930 --> 28:56.770
I'm with him.

28:56.770 --> 28:59.130
People on Earth are so
stubborn and conservative...

28:59.130 --> 29:02.510
...but don't have a problem
changing wives or husbands.

29:02.900 --> 29:05.550
And that's why I think
Char is trying to...

29:05.550 --> 29:08.260
...do what he can to bring out
the potential of humanity.

29:08.260 --> 29:09.930
I'm not so sure.

29:09.930 --> 29:13.350
That gives him the right to
plunge Earth into a freeze?

29:14.910 --> 29:16.230
I don't know...!

29:21.710 --> 29:25.310
Do you think Char will go through
with this plan to freeze the Earth?

29:25.310 --> 29:28.320
He's already started the process.

29:28.320 --> 29:30.620
In order to send Earth
into a total Ice Age...

29:30.620 --> 29:33.410
...he must crash another
asteroid onto the planet.

29:33.410 --> 29:38.170
But the Federation Forces control
everything within moon's orbit.

29:38.170 --> 29:39.670
That's why...

29:39.670 --> 29:42.630
...he's pushing to get Sweetwater
recognized as Neo Zeon territory.

29:42.630 --> 29:45.010
You think Adenauer Paraya
is here for negotiations?

29:45.010 --> 29:47.340
Yeah, I believe so.

29:47.340 --> 29:51.510
Char once joined our fight against
the Federation forces...

29:51.510 --> 29:54.680
...but he learned about those
people who live on Earth...

29:54.680 --> 29:56.730
...to the point where
he truly hates them.

29:56.730 --> 29:58.480
Yes, I realize that.

29:58.830 --> 30:03.230
So now he wants to settle it,
once and for all.

30:03.230 --> 30:04.740
But why?

30:05.090 --> 30:05.820
Hey.

30:12.390 --> 30:14.660
I'm relieved you got us here in time.

30:14.660 --> 30:16.830
Thanks to that, Earth can be saved.

30:16.830 --> 30:18.500
Good luck with
your negotiations, sir.

30:18.500 --> 30:21.290
Negotiations?
With whom? Where?

30:21.520 --> 30:24.170
You give orders to the
Space Forces from Lhasa.

30:24.170 --> 30:27.510
I can't imagine you came
out here for sightseeing.

30:27.510 --> 30:29.390
No one must know I'm here...

30:29.390 --> 30:33.010
...until the Federation Government
makes an official announcement.

30:33.010 --> 30:34.100
Sir!

30:34.780 --> 30:36.060
See ya!

30:37.200 --> 30:38.740
Welcome, sir.

30:38.740 --> 30:41.400
I'm Cameron Bloom
from the Audit Bureau.

30:41.400 --> 30:42.540
Thank you.

30:42.540 --> 30:43.570
Be careful now!

30:43.570 --> 30:44.860
Wow!

30:44.860 --> 30:45.440
Quess!

30:45.440 --> 30:46.910
Crew dismissed!

30:46.910 --> 30:49.570
Captain Bright Noa, huh?

30:49.570 --> 30:52.030
I wonder how things
are going with Mirai.

30:52.030 --> 30:54.620
There's a lot of work to do!

30:58.640 --> 31:01.210
The sample frame from
Mr. October arrived below.

31:01.210 --> 31:03.000
Oh, good.

31:03.640 --> 31:06.170
Hey, can we see the inside
of the Colony from here?

31:06.170 --> 31:07.210
Sure we can.

31:07.210 --> 31:10.320
I think that new frame
is a good idea.

31:10.320 --> 31:12.490
That Adenauer Paraya...

31:12.490 --> 31:16.600
He orders the Londo-Bell unit to
search out the remnants of Zeon...

31:16.600 --> 31:18.810
...and meanwhile,
he's off talking to Char.

31:18.810 --> 31:20.940
But that's what politicians do.

31:20.940 --> 31:22.560
Is that acceptable?

31:22.560 --> 31:24.060
Not really.

31:24.060 --> 31:25.570
The Colony!

31:26.880 --> 31:27.940
That's right.

31:27.940 --> 31:32.320
This is an old city
with about 5 million people.

31:35.970 --> 31:38.370
You're usually very nice,
just like this.

31:38.370 --> 31:40.540
But once in a while,
you become so cold.

31:40.540 --> 31:41.620
You think so?

31:41.620 --> 31:43.000
I do.

32:01.290 --> 32:03.310
We're pleased you could
come over here.

32:03.310 --> 32:06.740
Our pleasure. I'd like to
welcome you to Londenion.

32:06.740 --> 32:09.240
<i>These are Neo Zeon peoplel</i>

32:09.240 --> 32:11.610
You don't mind me taking Amuro?

32:11.610 --> 32:12.530
That's fine.

32:12.530 --> 32:15.630
We spend a lot of time together
when you're not around.

32:15.630 --> 32:17.230
Hathaway!

32:17.230 --> 32:18.330
Dad!

32:19.930 --> 32:23.120
Tell her not to bother me
about asking you out on a date.

32:23.120 --> 32:24.000
Quess?

32:24.000 --> 32:25.380
I've been looking for you!

32:25.380 --> 32:27.800
They wouldn't let me
call the battleship directly.

32:27.800 --> 32:30.010
I'm really sorry I had
to bug the Captain!

32:30.010 --> 32:31.010
That's okay!

32:31.010 --> 32:32.340
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

32:32.860 --> 32:35.010
Has he been re-charged?

32:35.010 --> 32:36.980
Yes! Bring him out.

32:36.980 --> 32:38.850
Sure! You mean Haro?

32:38.850 --> 32:40.180
Drake Hotel?

32:40.180 --> 32:40.810
Mr. Amuro?

32:41.330 --> 32:43.890
The Supreme Leader is here?!

32:47.870 --> 32:51.070
As this is a favor to us,
it's only natural...

32:51.070 --> 32:54.900
...to have our top official here
as a matter of courtesy.

32:54.900 --> 32:59.160
Your presence indeed
puts our minds at ease.

32:59.160 --> 33:00.330
Thank you.

33:00.330 --> 33:02.290
That's good to hear.

33:02.290 --> 33:05.420
I trust the treaty document
is genuine?

33:05.420 --> 33:06.770
Of course.

33:06.770 --> 33:11.050
Our government moved its HQ
before Fifth Luna hit Lhasa...

33:11.050 --> 33:15.430
...and put together what we
consider an official document.

33:15.430 --> 33:17.450
<i>What treaty?</i>

33:17.450 --> 33:20.100
If you'll accept the
conditions of the treaty...

33:20.100 --> 33:23.910
...we will hand over the
asteroid Axis to Neo Zeon.

33:23.910 --> 33:25.140
<i>What?</i>

33:26.440 --> 33:27.480
Haaaa-ro!

33:27.480 --> 33:28.900
Haro!

33:28.900 --> 33:30.120
Hathaway!

33:30.120 --> 33:31.280
Yes?!

33:35.090 --> 33:37.570
I heard about Haro
from my mother.

33:37.570 --> 33:39.410
He's third generation.
Look after him.

33:39.410 --> 33:40.660
Of course!

33:44.100 --> 33:49.540
First we surrender our Neo Zeon
fleet to the asteroid base Luna II?

33:49.540 --> 33:53.380
Otherwise we can't move
Axis to Sweetwater?

33:53.380 --> 33:57.720
Unless you agree on the conditions,
I can see no peace between us.

33:57.720 --> 33:59.240
Gold bars...

33:59.240 --> 34:00.600
What's this?

34:01.570 --> 34:04.560
Please review our
payment for Axis.

34:04.560 --> 34:06.740
That man is here
from the Audit Bureau.

34:06.740 --> 34:07.770
Sir!

34:07.770 --> 34:11.150
With this exchange, we have
officially purchased Axis.

34:11.150 --> 34:14.320
Another favor we ask is that
you allow our fleet to handle...

34:14.320 --> 34:17.130
...the transport of
Axis to Sweetwater.

34:17.130 --> 34:18.570
Why is that?

34:18.570 --> 34:21.280
When the fleet crews
no longer have jobs...

34:21.280 --> 34:24.610
...we're not in a position
to give severance pay.

34:24.610 --> 34:26.330
I see.

34:26.330 --> 34:27.620
That's a problem.

34:27.620 --> 34:28.710
Very well, then.

34:28.710 --> 34:31.290
We'll find them work within
the Federation Forces.

34:31.290 --> 34:35.130
And the nuclear engines in
Axis are fully operational...

34:35.130 --> 34:37.710
...so transport shouldn't
be a problem.

34:37.710 --> 34:40.180
You mean the old engines
can still be used?

34:40.180 --> 34:42.270
That's a relief!

34:42.270 --> 34:43.890
Excuse me.

34:46.280 --> 34:48.390
Bunch of snobs.

34:48.390 --> 34:52.940
If the Londo-Bell scoundrels
were to find out we're here...

34:52.940 --> 34:54.320
...they wouldn't take it so well.

34:54.320 --> 34:56.150
Certainly.

35:01.220 --> 35:04.830
<i>Amuro. I'm dolng somethlng
extremely wlcked.</i>

35:04.830 --> 35:07.960
<i>If you're nearby, feel my presence.</i>

35:09.810 --> 35:11.330
I'm not going into the city.

35:11.330 --> 35:12.250
Sir!

35:14.690 --> 35:16.510
Hail Zeon.

35:16.510 --> 35:17.840
Hail Zeon.

35:27.700 --> 35:29.980
Awesome!

35:31.580 --> 35:34.560
Chase that swan over there, Amuro!

36:03.070 --> 36:04.140
You!

36:04.390 --> 36:05.390
What's the matter, sir?!

36:05.390 --> 36:06.810
- Get Gyunei for me!
- Right!

36:10.160 --> 36:11.730
What are you doing here?!

36:11.730 --> 36:15.360
Unlike you, I'm more than
just a pilot!

36:15.360 --> 36:16.610
Come back!

36:25.050 --> 36:26.990
So, that's Char...

36:26.990 --> 36:30.660
We fought together, Char!
Why do you want to destroy Earth?!

36:31.100 --> 36:34.250
The people on Earth
do nothing but pollute it.

36:34.250 --> 36:36.630
Their souls are weighed
down by gravity.

36:37.770 --> 36:40.550
So, that's why parents
fight with each other.

36:48.160 --> 36:50.600
Char!

36:54.290 --> 36:55.850
Why?!

36:57.670 --> 37:00.420
Earth can't live with
all those parasites!

37:00.420 --> 37:03.780
Human wisdom can
overcome problems!

37:04.840 --> 37:08.620
Then, grant all those ignorant
people your so-called wisdom!

37:09.090 --> 37:11.330
He's right!
Because it can't be done...

37:14.500 --> 37:18.040
I'll do what you say
after I get rid of you!

37:21.560 --> 37:23.630
Amuro! You're not fighting fair!

37:23.630 --> 37:24.780
Quess!

37:24.780 --> 37:26.390
Shall we go?

37:27.030 --> 37:28.890
- Char!
- Quess!

37:37.450 --> 37:39.690
Captain!

37:44.500 --> 37:45.820
Quess!

37:49.050 --> 37:50.410
Quess!

37:50.410 --> 37:51.870
Hathaway...

37:55.540 --> 37:56.710
Char!

37:58.310 --> 38:00.000
Sorry to bother...

38:00.000 --> 38:02.480
I thought it might be you,
Mr. Cameron.

38:02.480 --> 38:03.510
Thank you.

38:03.510 --> 38:05.970
Why would someone from
the Audit Bureau want me?

38:05.970 --> 38:09.790
How is Mirai... Oh, excuse me...
How is your wife doing?

38:09.790 --> 38:12.180
I haven't seen her in six months.

38:12.180 --> 38:14.600
She's been living on Earth
this whole time.

38:14.600 --> 38:16.020
Oh, I see.

38:16.020 --> 38:17.530
Is there something?

38:17.530 --> 38:21.560
At first, I wasn't sure who
I should inform about this.

38:21.560 --> 38:24.650
Char is in this Colony right now.

38:26.130 --> 38:27.110
What's that?

38:27.110 --> 38:31.910
Yes, Char Aznable met with
Federation officials here.

38:31.910 --> 38:33.790
With Adenauer Paraya?

38:34.220 --> 38:36.250
He wasn't the only one, though.

38:36.250 --> 38:38.250
There were several others.

38:38.250 --> 38:43.170
They believe they reached a
binding peace agreement with Char.

38:44.560 --> 38:46.050
That's...

38:50.690 --> 38:54.570
You've got good taste!
How much for the girl?

38:54.570 --> 38:58.270
Cut out the smart remarks.
This girl's spoken for.

39:02.120 --> 39:03.370
They're all here.

39:03.370 --> 39:05.480
Good, just in time.

39:07.420 --> 39:11.620
We're heading out now into space.
What do you wish to do, Quess?

39:12.510 --> 39:14.180
Report on the Feddie Forces?!

39:14.180 --> 39:16.080
Still no movement.

39:16.080 --> 39:18.640
Some hag on the Ra-Cailum
cramps my style.

39:18.640 --> 39:20.540
Is that so? Well, then...

39:38.080 --> 39:39.060
What is it?

39:39.060 --> 39:40.980
You don't know what Char's up to!

39:40.980 --> 39:43.190
We had to sell the Axis asteroid...

39:43.190 --> 39:46.320
...the money will be used to
fulfill our welfare policies!

39:46.320 --> 39:49.880
Besides, Char said he'd
wipe out some Colonies!

39:49.880 --> 39:52.030
He'd never harm the Colonies.

39:52.030 --> 39:54.750
Char only wants to wipe out
all those who remain on Earth.

39:54.750 --> 39:58.260
I'm going to Luna II to prepare
for Neo Zeon's disarmament.

39:58.260 --> 40:00.160
Disarm their fleet?!

40:00.160 --> 40:03.330
Why won't you engage
Londo-Bell to oversee it?!

40:05.480 --> 40:06.550
Careful, sir.

40:07.190 --> 40:08.960
Oh. Could I borrow a phone?

40:08.960 --> 40:10.170
Yes, sir.

40:11.280 --> 40:13.940
We can't have Char's fleet
come close to any Colony.

40:13.940 --> 40:15.350
Vice-Minister.

40:15.350 --> 40:19.060
Then we will act independently
to monitor the situation.

40:19.060 --> 40:20.430
Yes, of course!

40:20.430 --> 40:23.850
If you officers determine a threat
to Earth, then make a move.

40:24.520 --> 40:27.070
Why isn't Quess
answering her phone?

40:27.070 --> 40:29.110
Captain, pass on a message for me.

40:29.110 --> 40:31.360
Tell her to remain
at the hotel for a few days.

40:31.360 --> 40:32.740
Yes, sir.

40:35.800 --> 40:37.330
I'm closing it.

40:41.600 --> 40:43.000
I'm floating.

40:44.680 --> 40:45.630
With this...

40:45.630 --> 40:46.670
Yes, I know.

40:46.670 --> 40:49.190
It's a bit older than the Jegan,
but I know.

40:49.190 --> 40:50.210
Are you sure?

40:50.210 --> 40:51.840
Like this?

40:53.070 --> 40:54.130
Wow!

40:54.130 --> 40:55.720
Bring the SSE in front of you.

40:59.990 --> 41:01.680
Is this really your first time?

41:01.680 --> 41:03.310
Here! A forward flip!

41:05.700 --> 41:06.940
What?!

41:06.940 --> 41:08.110
Is that Quess?

41:08.110 --> 41:10.320
Yes. Looks like she's a natural.

41:14.050 --> 41:16.070
The Musaka's ready to pick us up.

41:17.320 --> 41:19.090
Vroom!

41:19.090 --> 41:20.580
Stop!

41:21.850 --> 41:23.410
What's that?!

41:24.220 --> 41:26.290
Don't approach until they say so.

41:26.290 --> 41:27.710
It's okay!

41:32.610 --> 41:34.220
Quit it for my sake!

41:34.220 --> 41:37.720
There are already people out
there who hate me because...

41:37.720 --> 41:39.570
...I'm from the Newtype Labs.

41:39.570 --> 41:41.390
Leave those fools to me.

41:48.250 --> 41:52.820
You must have had some terrible
memories for you to hate Earth...

41:52.820 --> 41:54.280
...Quess Air?

41:55.960 --> 41:58.800
Why were you drawn to me?

41:58.800 --> 42:04.100
You said that the human soul
was weighed down by gravity.

42:04.100 --> 42:07.170
Those words reflect
exactly how I feel.

42:07.560 --> 42:08.330
But, you know...

42:08.580 --> 42:13.510
...I think that people who really
understand that are kind of tragic.

42:13.720 --> 42:16.650
I'm just walking the path
that I truly believe in.

42:16.650 --> 42:19.140
I saw a swan fly.

42:19.140 --> 42:22.260
And then Amuro shouted,
and then I also shouted.

42:22.260 --> 42:24.400
Then you appeared right after that.

42:24.400 --> 42:26.810
Is that why you betrayed
Amuro and the others?

42:28.450 --> 42:31.440
I met them by coincidence.

42:31.440 --> 42:34.360
I mean, I wasn't really even
friends with them or anything.

42:37.670 --> 42:40.260
It's hard to get an
operator's license for space.

42:40.260 --> 42:42.280
If I work at the Colony P. C...

42:42.280 --> 42:44.330
...I won't go hungry doing
those repair jobs.

42:44.330 --> 42:46.540
I just need training.

42:51.180 --> 42:53.500
You want it on a
fifty-month loan, right?

42:53.500 --> 42:57.020
Uh, right!

42:57.020 --> 42:58.590
Ouch!

43:00.990 --> 43:02.930
After only four or five tries!

43:02.930 --> 43:03.810
She's the real thing.

43:03.810 --> 43:04.680
That's right.

43:04.680 --> 43:08.770
Quess' brainwaves sync perfectly
with psycommu.

43:08.770 --> 43:11.020
- Quess, you know your target?
- Yes!

43:11.460 --> 43:14.070
The funnels will automatically
advance to the mark.

43:14.070 --> 43:15.160
Okay!

43:15.160 --> 43:17.570
- Deploy the funnels.
- Sure!

43:20.840 --> 43:24.910
You mean I can control those
with just my brainwaves?

43:24.910 --> 43:26.950
Picture the target.

43:26.950 --> 43:28.120
Picture it?

43:30.060 --> 43:31.420
Go! Funnels!

43:33.480 --> 43:35.880
Next, order the funnels to attack.

43:36.480 --> 43:38.630
<i>Order the funnels?</i>

43:44.200 --> 43:45.640
That's it!

43:45.640 --> 43:47.310
Funnels!

43:55.870 --> 43:57.690
Just like her.

44:07.700 --> 44:10.580
Would you mind?

44:11.350 --> 44:13.040
Here. For the leader.

44:14.060 --> 44:15.170
For the leader.

44:15.170 --> 44:16.500
For the Captain?

44:16.500 --> 44:18.800
From over there, to you.

44:18.800 --> 44:20.190
Thank you.

44:20.190 --> 44:21.300
Hail Zeon!

44:21.300 --> 44:23.010
Hail Zeon!

44:23.010 --> 44:25.970
Hail Zeon! Hail Zeon!

44:25.970 --> 44:29.810
High hopes and noble endeavors...

44:29.810 --> 44:34.020
...will shine with all
the twinkling stars.

44:34.020 --> 44:38.190
We hold you next to us...

44:38.190 --> 44:42.530
The galaxy, so glorious.

44:42.530 --> 44:46.660
We'll build with our dreams...

44:46.660 --> 44:51.250
A new world that bravely shines.

44:51.250 --> 44:54.710
Char is fighting for our prayers!

44:54.710 --> 45:00.170
Char is fighting for our prayers!

45:01.270 --> 45:04.050
So you're not pretending
to be leader.

45:04.050 --> 45:05.300
Is that funny?

45:05.300 --> 45:06.720
No.

45:07.110 --> 45:09.160
And are you going
to destroy Earth?

45:09.160 --> 45:11.270
I won't destroy it.

45:11.270 --> 45:13.770
I'm just giving the planet Earth
a nice long rest.

45:13.770 --> 45:15.810
Oh. That's what you want.

45:15.810 --> 45:18.230
Did the training give you
any headaches?

45:18.230 --> 45:20.480
No! I'm fine!

45:23.420 --> 45:25.820
Gyunei. I'm relying on you
for tomorrow's operation.

45:25.820 --> 45:27.490
Yes, sir.

45:29.260 --> 45:32.830
You're fine? Tomorrow's
operation is no field trip.

45:32.830 --> 45:33.710
You bet!

45:35.520 --> 45:37.040
Captain...!

45:38.060 --> 45:40.590
Get some rest tonight.

45:40.980 --> 45:42.280
Go.

45:42.280 --> 45:44.840
Just ramming Axis into the Earth...

45:44.840 --> 45:48.450
...will cause the same calamity
as that of a nuclear winter.

45:48.450 --> 45:53.100
That's an evil scheme no dictator
in history has ever attempted.

45:55.490 --> 45:58.020
Are you okay with that,
Captain Char?

45:58.500 --> 46:02.030
It's too late for lectures, Nanai.

46:02.420 --> 46:06.810
I believe in the rebirth of a
humanity that lives in space.

46:06.810 --> 46:11.870
However, in order to develop
all of us into Newtypes...

46:12.390 --> 46:16.240
...someone has to shoulder
all the evils of humanity.

46:16.240 --> 46:18.210
And you're okay with that?

46:20.020 --> 46:23.960
You thought up this latest plan...

46:23.960 --> 46:26.220
...to get even with Amuro, right?

46:26.220 --> 46:29.220
Do you think I'd be so petty?

46:29.820 --> 46:33.220
Amuro Ray wrongly believes
that compassion...

46:33.220 --> 46:35.370
...to be the weapon of a Newtype.

46:35.370 --> 46:38.690
A woman may be able
to forgive such a man.

46:38.690 --> 46:41.940
But, Captain, you cannot
forgive that about Amuro.

46:44.670 --> 46:47.570
During the War for
Zeon independence...

46:47.570 --> 46:50.950
...I had a protégé, a young pilot
named Lalah Sune.

46:50.950 --> 46:55.500
She found compassion in Amuro,
even though he was the enemy.

46:55.500 --> 46:59.870
Such deep mutual understanding is
only possible between Newtypes.

47:03.020 --> 47:05.510
- Lalah!
- Amuro!

47:05.920 --> 47:08.620
Lalah!
Stop playing around with him!

47:08.620 --> 47:10.010
Captain! Don't do it!

47:10.220 --> 47:11.640
What?!

47:12.650 --> 47:16.770
If only my sister Artesia
hadn't been there.

47:19.080 --> 47:20.060
Oh, no!

47:20.060 --> 47:21.520
Lalah!

47:26.210 --> 47:27.990
Lalah...!

47:31.530 --> 47:34.410
Oh, I wanted you to guide me.

47:35.590 --> 47:38.620
<i>All because she could tap
Into people's thoughts.</i>

47:38.620 --> 47:40.120
What's the matter?

47:41.540 --> 47:44.710
Those who are too much alike
will end up hating each other.

47:44.710 --> 47:48.920
They say love and hate
are two sides of the same coin

47:49.400 --> 47:51.050
I suppose so.

47:51.050 --> 47:53.390
I'm counting on you
for tomorrow's operation.

47:54.400 --> 47:58.310
I'll go on ahead to Axis
and wait for you there.

48:02.750 --> 48:06.270
And you're okay with
involving Quess?

48:06.960 --> 48:10.490
She really doesn't need to be
cyber-enhanced any further.

48:10.490 --> 48:11.450
Right.

48:11.450 --> 48:16.130
She's a Newtype that doesn't need
a psyco-frame to control funnels.

48:16.130 --> 48:17.540
Yes, she is special.

48:22.310 --> 48:25.590
Since he's decided to succeed
his father, Zeon Deikun...

48:25.590 --> 48:28.340
...taking on the name
must've changed him.

48:30.760 --> 48:33.800
How could he fall for such a brat?

48:35.150 --> 48:38.970
The war is just an outlet for
him to take out his frustrations.

48:38.970 --> 48:40.810
What do you mean?

48:40.810 --> 48:43.020
When people like
the Captain get angry...

48:43.020 --> 48:45.100
...they start destroying Colonies.

48:45.100 --> 48:48.110
Someone's got to be there
to prevent that.

48:48.110 --> 48:51.320
That's why I had them cyber-
enhance me into a Newtype.

48:51.320 --> 48:56.160
Both my parents died when
their Colony was wiped out.

48:56.630 --> 48:58.330
Bunch of morons!

48:59.180 --> 49:01.000
So, you want to be a psychic?

49:01.000 --> 49:02.000
Yeah.

49:02.000 --> 49:04.620
But I now realize that
I'll never be like you...

49:04.620 --> 49:07.460
...if I just get the enhancing
process at the Newtype Labs.

49:07.020 --> 49:11.970
So I want to be with you and
study you for as long as it takes.

49:11.970 --> 49:13.840
You asking me out?

49:13.840 --> 49:15.430
Are you bothered about my age?

49:16.240 --> 49:18.260
Hey. You're jealous, right?

49:18.260 --> 49:19.810
Because I like the Captain?

49:20.050 --> 49:22.100
That's not it!

49:23.490 --> 49:24.850
Quess!

49:25.060 --> 49:28.060
- Let's get him!
- Stop it!

49:28.870 --> 49:31.420
Ouch! That's not fair!

49:31.420 --> 49:34.070
So, there're no shuttles
for a while?

49:34.070 --> 49:36.910
The shuttle company plans
to leave Hong Kong.

49:37.340 --> 49:39.800
Is the news about a
peace treaty a lie?

49:39.800 --> 49:42.550
I hear Hong Kong
is the next target.

49:42.550 --> 49:43.750
Will a meteoroid hit Earth?

49:43.930 --> 49:45.500
Char would do it.

49:45.500 --> 49:49.040
I know because I fought
against him a long time ago.

49:49.040 --> 49:51.300
People on Earth don't know
what they're doing.

49:51.300 --> 49:54.950
Char is just too much
of a perfectionist.

49:54.950 --> 49:57.760
Colony Sweetwater was built...

49:57.760 --> 50:00.970
...by patching together a closed
type to an open type...

50:00.970 --> 50:03.770
...and is therefore very unstable.

50:03.770 --> 50:07.730
It was made hastily
in order to accommodate...

50:07.730 --> 50:10.770
...those refugees who had
survived past space wars.

50:11.750 --> 50:17.070
This was the only measure
taken by the Earth Federation.

50:17.070 --> 50:19.200
They concluded that this
would suffice.

50:19.200 --> 50:24.750
They remained on Earth and
refused to share the planet.

50:25.760 --> 50:28.210
My father, Zeon Deikun...

50:28.210 --> 50:29.750
...had made a request to Earth...

50:29.750 --> 50:33.670
...for autonomy for all space
emigrants, known as "Spacenoids."

50:33.670 --> 50:36.720
But he was assassinated
by the Zabi Family!

50:36.720 --> 50:40.550
The Zabis called themselves
the Principality of Zeon...

50:40.550 --> 50:44.060
...and launched a war of
independence against Earth!

50:44.660 --> 50:49.940
You know how it was to end,
with the Zabis losing the war.

50:49.940 --> 50:51.020
Fine and well.

50:51.020 --> 50:54.570
But the Earth government
had grown arrogant.

50:54.570 --> 50:57.900
The Federation Forces had
become corrupt from within...

50:58.070 --> 51:00.410
...giving rise to rogue movements...

51:00.410 --> 51:04.490
...including the Haman, who
claimed succession to the Zabis!

51:04.490 --> 51:06.700
This history has
made us refugees!

51:06.700 --> 51:09.370
I knew all that.

51:09.370 --> 51:11.380
I have come to believe...

51:11.380 --> 51:17.260
...that we must do everything to
prevent war from happening again!

51:17.730 --> 51:22.550
This is the true purpose behind our
operation to drop Axis onto Earth!

51:23.360 --> 51:26.980
As such, we will discipline those
who continue to live on Earth...

51:26.980 --> 51:29.940
...and eliminate the source of
any wars in the Earth's sphere!

51:29.940 --> 51:31.600
Hail! Hail!

51:33.000 --> 51:34.320
Captain!

51:34.320 --> 51:36.190
You're the savior of Sweetwater!

51:38.170 --> 51:42.240
But aren't they disarming
themselves at Luna II?

51:44.630 --> 51:46.200
Everyone!

51:46.200 --> 51:48.540
So that we may forge
our own path...

51:48.540 --> 51:51.670
...and establish a government
for the refugees...

51:51.670 --> 51:57.010
I ask you to lend me your great
strength for just a little longer!

51:57.010 --> 51:58.970
When we've succeeded...

51:58.970 --> 52:01.010
...I will then be able
to join my father, Zeon!

52:01.010 --> 52:04.220
Hail! Hail!

52:19.750 --> 52:21.610
The Rewloola, right?

52:21.610 --> 52:23.780
Do you think they'll be
fooled by these dummy ships?

52:23.990 --> 52:28.620
As long as those Feddies see
the correct number of ships.

52:28.620 --> 52:31.580
Our fleet with the dummies
are to attack Luna II.

52:31.580 --> 52:35.380
And you will occupy Axis while
all this is transpiring, Captain.

52:35.380 --> 52:38.670
If all goes well, we'll use the
nuclear weapons from Luna II.

52:38.670 --> 52:39.340
Right.

52:39.340 --> 52:44.180
Both to accelerate Axis,
and to contaminate the Earth.

53:04.210 --> 53:09.120
How many nuclear weapons from
past centuries are stored at Luna II?

53:09.680 --> 53:11.410
There's enough payload...

53:11.410 --> 53:14.250
...to annihilate the Neo Zeon
fleet a hundred times over.

53:14.250 --> 53:16.670
Char is aware of that fact.

53:16.670 --> 53:18.460
He's a very clever man.

53:18.460 --> 53:21.920
Are you implying that our
Londo-Bell is itching for a war?

53:21.920 --> 53:24.760
I am.
It does look that way from Earth.

53:24.760 --> 53:26.010
Vice-Minister.

53:26.010 --> 53:28.050
There's a broadcast
from Sweetwater.

53:28.050 --> 53:29.610
Put it up.

53:29.610 --> 53:31.870
How's the signal?

53:31.870 --> 53:33.390
Perfect.

53:35.190 --> 53:37.810
Their flagship Rewloola
is at the rear.

53:37.810 --> 53:39.520
Numbers match, sir!

53:39.520 --> 53:41.940
Wait! There's one extra vessel!

53:41.940 --> 53:44.450
Shows you how honest Char is.

53:44.800 --> 53:48.410
I guess the only thing left to
worry about are space aliens.

53:48.410 --> 53:51.330
I wonder if there'll be jobs
for us when this is over.

53:51.330 --> 53:55.210
On Earth, they're always looking
for people to clean the beaches.

53:55.210 --> 53:58.350
Our glorious Neo Zeon fleet!

53:58.350 --> 54:00.630
It's difficult for us to part with you.

54:00.630 --> 54:05.090
But we shall keep your memories
in our minds and make...

54:06.400 --> 54:08.680
So, there were fifteen
nuclear warheads...

54:08.680 --> 54:10.970
...in addition to the ones in Luna II?

54:11.530 --> 54:15.020
But considering they're under
the Audit Bureau's jurisdiction...

54:15.020 --> 54:16.980
...I'd say they're virtual antiques.

54:16.980 --> 54:18.480
Please be careful.

54:18.480 --> 54:20.610
Aren't your actions
considered a crime?

54:20.610 --> 54:24.650
If this Federation government
survives, I'll get life imprisonment.

54:24.650 --> 54:26.200
You're fine with that?

54:26.200 --> 54:29.030
I want to see Mirai alive.

54:29.030 --> 54:31.090
That's why I'm doing this.

54:31.090 --> 54:34.160
You were once her fiancé.
I understand.

54:34.160 --> 54:35.500
Thank you.

54:35.500 --> 54:37.290
This Neo Zeon broadcast.

54:37.290 --> 54:41.380
Is their claim that the entire fleet
has left for disarmament a sham?

54:41.380 --> 54:42.750
Probably.

54:42.750 --> 54:44.630
It's all a big show.

54:49.110 --> 54:52.100
That Quess is on my tail!

54:56.410 --> 54:58.100
She's looking good!

54:58.100 --> 55:00.480
Navigation axle targeting Luna II...

55:00.480 --> 55:01.060
...fixed!

55:01.250 --> 55:02.360
Okay!

55:02.360 --> 55:05.110
All gun turrets,
maximum elevation!

55:05.710 --> 55:07.530
Bring in the Jagd-Doga.

55:17.390 --> 55:19.750
You kids taking part in the battle?

55:19.750 --> 55:20.710
Problem with that?!

55:20.710 --> 55:22.880
A big mouth for a fake Newtype.

55:22.880 --> 55:24.800
I am a real Newtype!

55:25.520 --> 55:27.340
Gyunei. Forget it.

55:27.340 --> 55:29.970
Just ignore those "normal people."

55:31.690 --> 55:32.510
Rezin!

55:32.510 --> 55:33.350
Stop it!

55:33.350 --> 55:35.930
Well, I guess you're not normal.

55:35.930 --> 55:36.720
That's right.

55:36.720 --> 55:38.810
How cute.

55:52.970 --> 55:55.160
Bring in Alpha-Azieru!

55:55.160 --> 55:56.740
Fire the grappling cables!

56:09.020 --> 56:11.010
Neo Zeon fleet confirmed.

56:11.010 --> 56:13.390
Numbers same as when
they left Sweetwater.

56:13.390 --> 56:16.600
Captain! Why hasn't this
vessel moved up to the front?!

56:16.600 --> 56:18.060
We're insulting Char!

56:18.060 --> 56:21.850
I must first consider the safety
of officials like yourself!

56:23.080 --> 56:25.440
The fleet's spreading out laterally.

56:25.440 --> 56:27.280
They're supposed
to approach single file.

56:27.280 --> 56:29.280
Scout team, launch!

56:34.380 --> 56:36.120
We'll commence our attack.

56:36.120 --> 56:37.080
Yes, sir!

56:42.890 --> 56:46.750
Launch mobile suits 30 seconds
after commencing barrage.

56:58.570 --> 57:00.180
Numerous heat sources!

57:00.180 --> 57:02.350
What?! Evade!

57:15.090 --> 57:18.120
But the treaty! This is crazy!

57:35.150 --> 57:36.090
Hey, Quess!

57:36.090 --> 57:38.260
Just get a feel for the battle.

57:38.260 --> 57:39.510
Follow me.

57:40.320 --> 57:41.430
Okay.

57:56.880 --> 57:58.070
Wow...

58:00.800 --> 58:02.620
Here they come.

58:10.730 --> 58:13.630
I'll take care of all these guys
on my own.

58:14.570 --> 58:16.130
They're here.

58:17.940 --> 58:18.890
Gyunei!

58:18.890 --> 58:20.640
Darn!

58:24.910 --> 58:28.020
This is war, huh? Gyunei...

58:31.540 --> 58:33.070
Go away!

58:39.840 --> 58:42.640
Our objective is to capture Luna II.

58:42.640 --> 58:44.540
Quess!

58:45.930 --> 58:48.960
There's another one
hiding over there!

58:50.060 --> 58:51.590
We've got to escape!

58:51.590 --> 58:54.510
- Our soldiers are getting killed!
- They're here!

58:54.860 --> 58:56.590
The enemy?!

58:57.230 --> 58:59.590
Down you go!

59:04.950 --> 59:07.140
I did it! I did it!

59:11.290 --> 59:12.900
Watch out! Quess!

59:14.290 --> 59:16.440
That damage won't
cause an explosion.

59:16.440 --> 59:17.780
You're safe.

59:32.690 --> 59:34.380
Take this.

59:40.860 --> 59:43.770
I'll wipe out the Feddies
on my own.

59:43.770 --> 59:45.890
Quess! Are you all right?!

59:52.040 --> 59:53.610
Wh-Why...

59:53.610 --> 59:56.230
Why do I feel so weird?

59:59.840 --> 01:00:02.660
We won without moving
to the combat bridge.

01:00:02.660 --> 01:00:05.410
Now we can deliver
Luna ll's nukes to the Captain.

01:00:05.410 --> 01:00:07.840
That'll keep us busy.

01:00:07.840 --> 01:00:11.170
Captain, your plan
worked flawlessly.

01:00:11.170 --> 01:00:12.750
Stop your crying.

01:00:12.750 --> 01:00:15.960
Oh, Cameron.
I'll leave him with you now.

01:00:15.960 --> 01:00:18.510
He must get that from Mirai.

01:00:18.510 --> 01:00:19.630
So sensitive.

01:00:19.630 --> 01:00:20.150
Good-bye.

01:00:20.150 --> 01:00:23.050
I pray that Luna II
hasn't been wiped out.

01:00:23.050 --> 01:00:24.390
Who knows?

01:00:30.330 --> 01:00:33.900
My big sob act sure got
me out of there.

01:00:45.050 --> 01:00:46.910
Check hull seals!

01:00:51.060 --> 01:00:54.630
Good thing I studied
the ship's layout.

01:00:56.060 --> 01:00:58.210
We have a problem with hatch 48!

01:00:58.210 --> 01:00:59.340
What's that?

01:00:59.340 --> 01:01:01.810
Huh? Problem corrected!

01:01:01.810 --> 01:01:04.720
Maintenance! Check out hatch 48!

01:01:04.720 --> 01:01:05.760
What's going on?

01:01:05.760 --> 01:01:07.260
Beats me.

01:01:14.370 --> 01:01:16.150
I'm going to test it!

01:01:17.870 --> 01:01:19.580
Stop fooling around.

01:01:19.580 --> 01:01:21.440
Move it to the Air Lock.

01:01:21.440 --> 01:01:22.360
Roger!

01:01:23.460 --> 01:01:24.680
Captain.

01:01:24.680 --> 01:01:25.740
What is it?

01:01:26.550 --> 01:01:28.490
- Don't you find it strange?
- What?

01:01:29.340 --> 01:01:32.620
Two fleets leave
Luna II and Londenion.

01:01:32.620 --> 01:01:36.870
Leaving at the same time,
we should arrive at Axis first.

01:01:36.870 --> 01:01:39.630
Why would Char be that foolish?

01:01:40.100 --> 01:01:43.340
But all their ships are at Luna II
right now, even an extra one.

01:01:43.340 --> 01:01:44.340
Exactly.

01:01:44.340 --> 01:01:45.340
What's up?

01:01:45.340 --> 01:01:47.600
Sweetwater's broadcast
was a hoax.

01:01:47.600 --> 01:01:48.760
What?

01:01:48.760 --> 01:01:49.600
Look here.

01:01:49.600 --> 01:01:52.100
They don't show us any close-ups...

01:01:52.100 --> 01:01:54.060
...and I can't see any gun barrels.

01:01:54.060 --> 01:01:55.350
They're dummy ships.

01:01:55.350 --> 01:01:56.940
Which means...

01:01:56.940 --> 01:01:58.690
Char has already made it to Axis.

01:02:14.220 --> 01:02:15.120
Okay!

01:02:15.120 --> 01:02:17.580
Mobile suit forces,
go and scout out Axis!

01:02:17.580 --> 01:02:19.290
Lyle! I'm going, too.

01:02:19.290 --> 01:02:20.380
Yes, sir!

01:02:27.320 --> 01:02:30.930
If Axis hits Earth with
all those Luna II warheads...

01:02:30.930 --> 01:02:32.810
...those elite snobs are goners.

01:02:32.810 --> 01:02:36.910
But the Londo-Bell fleet may
arrive at Axis before we do.

01:02:36.910 --> 01:02:38.560
That may be so, but...

01:02:38.560 --> 01:02:39.790
Huh?

01:02:39.790 --> 01:02:42.440
We're on combat alert,
and you're wearing that?!

01:02:42.440 --> 01:02:43.940
Stay out of here!

01:02:43.940 --> 01:02:45.940
I'm just taking a walk!

01:02:47.050 --> 01:02:49.820
Everybody's on edge while
we're on combat alert.

01:02:49.820 --> 01:02:51.120
You're right.

01:02:51.630 --> 01:02:53.620
This isn't a playground!

01:02:53.620 --> 01:02:54.910
Let me go!

01:02:54.910 --> 01:02:55.910
Quess!

01:02:56.720 --> 01:03:00.420
Get into your pilot suit, and
stand by at the assigned station.

01:03:11.800 --> 01:03:13.890
We haven't heard from Hathaway.

01:03:13.890 --> 01:03:16.980
Lines must be tied up
with emergency calls.

01:03:23.500 --> 01:03:27.150
Mom said it's about time
I get space experience.

01:03:27.750 --> 01:03:32.410
I have to hold out a bit longer,
or they'll dump me in a Colony.

01:03:35.140 --> 01:03:37.450
Looks good!

01:03:38.310 --> 01:03:38.870
Good!

01:03:39.080 --> 01:03:41.290
Now, I can finish off
Char by myself!

01:03:41.290 --> 01:03:43.420
Please stop talking that way!

01:03:43.420 --> 01:03:45.800
I'm worried you'll
get yourself hurt.

01:03:45.800 --> 01:03:49.260
Astonaige...
You, silly man.

01:03:49.260 --> 01:03:51.840
Identifying fleet!
They're Federation vessels!

01:03:59.390 --> 01:04:01.770
Was it a surprise attack?

01:04:06.070 --> 01:04:10.380
Everyone on the main bridge was
lost, including Adenauer Paraya.

01:04:10.380 --> 01:04:12.420
What about Char's fleet?

01:04:12.420 --> 01:04:15.910
They broke into Luna ll's
nuclear weapons cache.

01:04:16.390 --> 01:04:18.580
The Colony fleets won't help us.

01:04:18.580 --> 01:04:21.060
They're afraid of riots breaking out.

01:04:21.060 --> 01:04:25.440
It's as if the Colonies and Earth
were helping Char!

01:04:25.440 --> 01:04:29.300
Not all of Neo Zeon's
vessels are gathered at Axis!

01:04:29.300 --> 01:04:30.340
I'm going!

01:04:30.340 --> 01:04:33.260
Quess!
What're you going to do?!

01:04:33.780 --> 01:04:35.430
I can't stand that woman!

01:04:35.430 --> 01:04:38.180
She's a woman who
earned her position...

01:04:38.180 --> 01:04:40.770
...cause she's so close with the
Captain!

01:04:40.770 --> 01:04:42.850
I'm going to ask him about that!

01:04:44.040 --> 01:04:46.090
Don't get too close to the Captain!

01:04:46.090 --> 01:04:48.570
I don't want to hear
about your jealousy!

01:04:48.570 --> 01:04:50.080
I'm not jealous!

01:04:50.080 --> 01:04:51.400
Open the hatch!

01:04:51.630 --> 01:04:52.700
Nanai...

01:04:52.700 --> 01:04:54.210
It's up to you.

01:04:54.210 --> 01:04:56.910
Get that damaged
Jagd-Doga out of here!

01:05:07.480 --> 01:05:09.460
Prepare to fire decoy missiles!

01:05:09.460 --> 01:05:10.930
Preparing to fire missiles!

01:05:10.930 --> 01:05:13.470
Control will then be transferred
to the combat bridge!

01:05:13.470 --> 01:05:15.970
Minovsky particles
at combat density!

01:05:16.530 --> 01:05:19.100
All hands,
prepare for visual combat!

01:05:19.100 --> 01:05:20.890
Activate monitoring systems!

01:05:21.410 --> 01:05:23.560
First wave of missiles, launch!

01:05:31.250 --> 01:05:33.920
All hands, prepare for launch!
All hands...!

01:05:33.920 --> 01:05:35.610
Everyone in your team here?

01:05:38.220 --> 01:05:39.160
What the?

01:05:39.160 --> 01:05:41.040
Follow Kayra's Re-GZ!

01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:42.540
Haro!

01:05:42.540 --> 01:05:44.210
Where's your normal suit?!

01:05:44.210 --> 01:05:45.830
You want to suffocate?!

01:05:45.830 --> 01:05:46.820
Amuro...

01:05:46.820 --> 01:05:47.920
Hathaway!

01:05:47.920 --> 01:05:49.790
A-Amuro...

01:05:49.790 --> 01:05:51.380
I'll take care of this.

01:05:51.380 --> 01:05:53.590
You'll be leading the first wave.
You'd better go.

01:05:53.590 --> 01:05:54.340
Right.

01:05:54.650 --> 01:05:56.340
Opening hatch in 5 minutes!

01:05:56.340 --> 01:05:58.720
Check normal suits!

01:05:59.030 --> 01:06:00.700
Second wave now! Go!

01:06:00.700 --> 01:06:02.390
- Second wave, fire!
- Roger!

01:06:04.950 --> 01:06:06.690
Heat sources approaching!

01:06:06.690 --> 01:06:07.770
Prepare for counterattack!

01:06:07.980 --> 01:06:09.770
Open combat bridge!

01:06:09.770 --> 01:06:11.570
Contact the Captain!

01:06:16.710 --> 01:06:19.480
They've finally come, huh?

01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:22.160
Start ignition when you're
done with the pulse thrusters.

01:06:22.160 --> 01:06:24.290
Please hold them back
for another ten minutes.

01:06:24.290 --> 01:06:25.580
Roger that.

01:06:30.270 --> 01:06:32.630
They're later than I expected.

01:06:35.480 --> 01:06:38.550
Launch attack from the
north side of Axis!

01:06:38.550 --> 01:06:40.180
Watch for friendly fire!

01:06:41.110 --> 01:06:42.260
Is that it?

01:07:02.430 --> 01:07:03.790
Destroy them!

01:07:07.970 --> 01:07:10.750
A nuclear warhead
amongst their missiles...

01:07:10.750 --> 01:07:12.380
Not bad, Londo-Bell.

01:07:15.400 --> 01:07:16.630
Second wave's coming!

01:07:19.360 --> 01:07:21.430
Your mother and sister would be...

01:07:21.430 --> 01:07:23.600
...worried sick if they knew
you're in the battlefield!

01:07:23.600 --> 01:07:25.770
That's not a bad thing for a boy.

01:07:25.770 --> 01:07:26.930
It's no joke!

01:07:27.410 --> 01:07:30.380
You want to see Quess, don't you?
Hathaway?

01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:32.810
I'm going to get her back!

01:07:32.810 --> 01:07:34.190
Hathaway...

01:07:34.790 --> 01:07:35.960
We're launching at once.

01:07:35.960 --> 01:07:37.320
Right.

01:07:37.880 --> 01:07:42.190
Char is taking advantage of
Quess' very sensitive nature.

01:07:42.190 --> 01:07:43.240
You won't beat him.

01:07:43.240 --> 01:07:45.040
Taking advantage of her?!

01:07:45.040 --> 01:07:47.290
Char is enhancing her abilities.

01:07:47.290 --> 01:07:49.290
And now she's become
one of his tools.

01:07:49.290 --> 01:07:50.470
No...

01:07:50.470 --> 01:07:54.040
Char dares to change the
world by destroying lives.

01:07:54.040 --> 01:07:56.210
If she's going to follow a man like
that...

01:07:56.210 --> 01:07:59.300
...she's just courting
the grim reaper until...

01:07:59.300 --> 01:08:01.050
Quess will not die!

01:08:01.050 --> 01:08:02.890
I'll bring her back!

01:08:02.890 --> 01:08:05.640
That's why I learned how
to work a mobile suit!

01:08:05.890 --> 01:08:09.940
With an attitude like that,
you'll be met with death yourself.

01:08:11.750 --> 01:08:14.270
First-wave mobile-suits
to launch immediately...

01:08:14.270 --> 01:08:16.150
...following fourth-wave missiles!

01:08:22.800 --> 01:08:23.910
Kayra!

01:08:23.910 --> 01:08:26.330
I'll make your favorite salad.

01:08:26.330 --> 01:08:27.800
I love you.

01:08:27.800 --> 01:08:29.370
Kayra in Re-GZ, taking off!

01:08:29.580 --> 01:08:31.000
What'd you say?!

01:08:46.360 --> 01:08:47.640
The second wave is here.

01:08:47.640 --> 01:08:50.350
Mobile suit forces,
go above the minefield.

01:09:05.280 --> 01:09:07.030
Time to go, Axis.

01:09:07.030 --> 01:09:10.450
Take your dreadful
memories with you!

01:09:23.730 --> 01:09:25.840
Still more?

01:09:37.250 --> 01:09:38.610
Beautiful!

01:09:41.630 --> 01:09:43.360
Axis engines firing up!

01:09:43.360 --> 01:09:45.410
Commencing descent to Earth!

01:09:45.410 --> 01:09:47.160
Launch fifth wave of missiles!

01:09:47.160 --> 01:09:47.780
Fire!

01:09:47.780 --> 01:09:49.740
All hands, combat status 1!

01:09:49.740 --> 01:09:51.120
Release dummy ships!

01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:53.120
Prepare evasive maneuvers!

01:10:00.270 --> 01:10:03.300
I'll contact you if
I need to speak to you.

01:10:03.300 --> 01:10:04.270
Okay.

01:10:04.270 --> 01:10:06.050
Hey, what's that thing?

01:10:06.050 --> 01:10:07.390
It's a psyco-frame.

01:10:07.390 --> 01:10:10.010
I'm doing tests to
learn its capabilities.

01:10:10.660 --> 01:10:11.850
Go on.

01:10:22.040 --> 01:10:24.650
Just one nuclear missile
among them?

01:10:24.650 --> 01:10:26.200
Lmpressive, Bright.

01:10:26.200 --> 01:10:28.320
Nanai. Hurry over here.

01:10:28.320 --> 01:10:30.280
If you don't want Quess hurt...

01:10:30.280 --> 01:10:32.620
...stick with her until
she finds Captain Char.

01:10:32.620 --> 01:10:33.330
Yes, ma'am!

01:10:33.330 --> 01:10:34.250
Skipper.

01:10:34.250 --> 01:10:35.460
Let him go.

01:10:35.460 --> 01:10:38.040
We're about to enter
the Axis combat zone.

01:10:41.770 --> 01:10:43.460
I don't care what anyone says.

01:10:43.460 --> 01:10:46.630
There's no way I'll lose
Quess to the Captain!

01:10:48.530 --> 01:10:50.220
This heat source is Axis.

01:10:50.220 --> 01:10:51.850
On the left, a nuclear explosion.

01:10:51.850 --> 01:10:54.680
There're so many dummies,
I can't count their ships.

01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.980
Then burn those dummies!

01:11:06.840 --> 01:11:08.820
That's Axis over there.

01:11:08.820 --> 01:11:10.490
The Captain's there!

01:11:13.220 --> 01:11:15.000
Captain...

01:11:16.810 --> 01:11:19.020
Heat source to starboard!
Enemy!

01:11:19.020 --> 01:11:21.040
Reinforcements from Luna II?

01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:27.970
Second wave, launch now.

01:11:27.970 --> 01:11:30.100
Support forces will cover the fleet.

01:11:30.100 --> 01:11:31.050
That's good.

01:11:33.450 --> 01:11:36.020
Gundam, let's do it!

01:11:38.740 --> 01:11:41.230
Continue cover fire
for another 30 seconds.

01:11:41.230 --> 01:11:43.190
Going by the book?

01:11:43.190 --> 01:11:44.940
I wish you the best.

01:11:44.940 --> 01:11:46.110
Thanks.

01:11:54.130 --> 01:11:57.700
Will their fleet intercept before
we destroy the nuclear thrusters?

01:12:10.860 --> 01:12:13.350
We've got to stop Axis!

01:12:17.200 --> 01:12:18.600
Those lights.

01:12:18.600 --> 01:12:21.020
Are you somewhere
within those circles of light?

01:12:27.670 --> 01:12:29.690
Quess is... Over there!

01:12:32.760 --> 01:12:34.410
Don't be stupid, Quess!

01:12:34.410 --> 01:12:35.530
Gyunei...

01:12:35.530 --> 01:12:38.330
The mobile suits are engaged
in battle north of Axis!

01:12:38.330 --> 01:12:39.080
Okay.

01:12:39.260 --> 01:12:40.540
Sixth wave!

01:12:40.540 --> 01:12:42.080
This is it! Don't miss!

01:12:48.730 --> 01:12:52.130
Londo-Bell, huh?
Should have stuck to ringing bells.

01:12:54.190 --> 01:12:56.140
You're getting on my nerves.

01:12:57.610 --> 01:12:58.890
There he is!

01:12:58.890 --> 01:13:02.060
Captain!
Why are you hiding over there?

01:13:03.660 --> 01:13:04.960
Quess.

01:13:04.960 --> 01:13:07.480
Londo-Bell mobile suits?

01:13:08.830 --> 01:13:10.490
Missiles?

01:13:13.200 --> 01:13:15.450
Th-They're nuclear missiles!

01:13:19.890 --> 01:13:21.410
Funnels.

01:13:21.410 --> 01:13:24.140
Aim at the most
intense heat sources.

01:13:24.140 --> 01:13:25.920
Hit them!

01:13:32.270 --> 01:13:33.630
All right!

01:13:37.650 --> 01:13:39.600
Awesome.

01:13:39.990 --> 01:13:41.440
Captain!

01:13:41.440 --> 01:13:44.440
Gyunei halted the
enemy nukes for us.

01:13:44.440 --> 01:13:47.060
That's what a cyber-Newtype
is supposed to do.

01:13:47.060 --> 01:13:47.900
Captain!

01:13:47.900 --> 01:13:49.980
Nanai slapped me real hard!

01:13:49.980 --> 01:13:51.820
I do hate violence.

01:13:51.820 --> 01:13:54.360
I'll talk to Nanai myself.
Quess?

01:14:00.840 --> 01:14:03.660
Quess, you're not
wearing a pilot suit.

01:14:03.660 --> 01:14:06.500
Will you really?
Make sure she's punished.

01:14:06.500 --> 01:14:08.000
Don't worry.

01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:09.840
Then, I'll do my job!

01:14:09.840 --> 01:14:11.130
Calm down.

01:14:11.130 --> 01:14:11.860
But...

01:14:11.860 --> 01:14:14.840
You haven't felt the terror
of real-life combat.

01:14:14.840 --> 01:14:15.720
Terror?

01:14:15.720 --> 01:14:16.720
Yeah.

01:14:17.610 --> 01:14:21.000
I felt kind of strange.
That's about it.

01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:22.660
It isn't fair.

01:14:22.660 --> 01:14:24.270
Nanai wasn't very nice to me.

01:14:24.520 --> 01:14:27.320
So you came to see me, right?

01:14:27.320 --> 01:14:28.750
Captain!

01:14:28.750 --> 01:14:30.520
Those feelings of yours.

01:14:30.520 --> 01:14:32.610
You could be a true Newtype.

01:14:32.610 --> 01:14:34.280
Good girl.

01:14:35.960 --> 01:14:37.410
I found it!

01:14:48.730 --> 01:14:51.130
They just got my fringe.

01:14:53.190 --> 01:14:55.970
I sense a presence from above-left.

01:14:57.360 --> 01:14:58.930
A Gundam?

01:15:09.580 --> 01:15:10.520
A dummy!

01:15:10.520 --> 01:15:11.650
There!

01:15:13.420 --> 01:15:14.900
This one's a real rock!

01:15:17.710 --> 01:15:20.110
Go around the rocks and
get him from both sides!

01:15:22.620 --> 01:15:24.740
I'm sure of it! That's a Gundam!

01:15:24.740 --> 01:15:27.620
If I destroy it, I'll prove I'm
stronger than Captain Char!

01:15:35.050 --> 01:15:36.210
There!

01:15:44.260 --> 01:15:47.140
Without the remote controls,
we'll have to go and shoot!

01:15:47.140 --> 01:15:48.310
Yeah, but...

01:15:48.310 --> 01:15:50.520
I'll... I'll do it!

01:15:50.520 --> 01:15:53.110
Miss Chan...
She sure can tough it out.

01:16:01.280 --> 01:16:02.450
What's wrong?

01:16:02.450 --> 01:16:05.200
We can't operate them
from Control!

01:16:05.200 --> 01:16:05.990
They're here!

01:16:10.180 --> 01:16:12.040
Who cares if they're Newtypes...

01:16:12.040 --> 01:16:14.290
...if they can't stop the fleet!

01:16:16.630 --> 01:16:18.300
I'm glad you found me.

01:16:18.300 --> 01:16:20.220
- A dummy!
- Right!

01:16:32.750 --> 01:16:33.900
This way!

01:16:35.520 --> 01:16:37.870
Wh-What is this power?!

01:16:37.870 --> 01:16:40.320
How could I be hit?!

01:16:42.960 --> 01:16:44.590
You did it!

01:16:44.590 --> 01:16:45.780
Not yet.

01:16:52.020 --> 01:16:55.670
It feels like people
are coming into me!

01:16:55.670 --> 01:16:58.250
I feel sick and scared!

01:17:05.030 --> 01:17:06.680
Quess...

01:17:11.580 --> 01:17:13.940
I'll get there first!

01:17:15.660 --> 01:17:16.610
That Feddie craft!

01:17:16.610 --> 01:17:18.980
Do you want to wipe out our fleet?

01:17:18.980 --> 01:17:20.280
You jerk!

01:17:21.170 --> 01:17:22.490
Kayra...!

01:17:23.340 --> 01:17:24.780
Got you now!

01:17:27.880 --> 01:17:31.930
I can get another shot off!
I want Axis!

01:17:31.930 --> 01:17:33.160
I'll get you!

01:17:41.300 --> 01:17:43.540
Gundam wannabe!

01:17:43.540 --> 01:17:45.340
I've got it!

01:17:45.340 --> 01:17:46.470
Oh, no!

01:17:46.470 --> 01:17:48.930
You've lost all your weapons.

01:17:48.930 --> 01:17:50.680
I'll grab the Gundam look-alike.

01:17:50.680 --> 01:17:51.600
Again!

01:17:58.540 --> 01:18:00.940
I'll use this one as bait.

01:18:04.750 --> 01:18:05.820
Wh-what is it?

01:18:05.820 --> 01:18:07.620
Stop playing with me.

01:18:07.620 --> 01:18:10.030
That presence again!

01:18:12.680 --> 01:18:15.830
The two Gundams.
Are they calling each other?

01:18:17.060 --> 01:18:19.340
The escape pod...!

01:18:19.810 --> 01:18:21.590
It won't work!

01:18:24.480 --> 01:18:26.050
Stay where you are!

01:18:26.050 --> 01:18:29.350
If you disobey me,
I'll kill this pilot!

01:18:29.350 --> 01:18:29.970
Amuro!

01:18:29.970 --> 01:18:33.180
The enemy's not moving!
Take him out!

01:18:35.060 --> 01:18:36.480
Kayra?!

01:18:40.480 --> 01:18:43.440
Amuro?
You're the famous Gundam pilot.

01:18:43.440 --> 01:18:44.780
Optical voice?

01:18:44.780 --> 01:18:49.030
If you surrender your Gundam,
I'll release this pilot to you.

01:18:49.590 --> 01:18:51.620
<i>What's wrong? Hurry upl</i>

01:18:51.620 --> 01:18:55.580
<i>Once I get that Nu Gundam,
I'll have the power to defeat Char...</i>

01:18:55.580 --> 01:18:58.830
<i>...then I'll be a man worthy
of taklng Quess for myselfl</i>

01:18:58.830 --> 01:19:00.290
Get him!

01:19:04.940 --> 01:19:06.630
You're trying to tow me?

01:19:06.630 --> 01:19:08.930
Signal your surrender,
and toss your rifle!

01:19:09.090 --> 01:19:10.970
Don't worry about me...!

01:19:10.970 --> 01:19:13.850
Stop it!
I'll detach my funnels!

01:19:14.820 --> 01:19:16.100
Yeah, right!

01:19:16.100 --> 01:19:17.850
Your radiator plates aren't a threat!

01:19:17.850 --> 01:19:20.020
Destroy Amuro!

01:19:23.320 --> 01:19:24.820
Again...!

01:19:24.820 --> 01:19:26.130
Amuro!

01:19:26.130 --> 01:19:27.240
Quess?

01:19:31.970 --> 01:19:34.580
You're resisting! Amuro!

01:19:38.160 --> 01:19:42.080
You're to blame for this.
You ignored my warnings!

01:19:45.100 --> 01:19:47.010
He has funnels?!

01:19:52.320 --> 01:19:54.510
Kayra...

01:20:05.120 --> 01:20:06.610
I...

01:20:06.610 --> 01:20:09.710
Seems the first wave pulled back.

01:20:09.710 --> 01:20:11.700
I feel like I'm going to explode.

01:20:11.700 --> 01:20:16.450
This girl senses everything
in the battlefield.

01:20:17.100 --> 01:20:19.830
Don't use up all of our
anti-missile particle shells!

01:20:19.830 --> 01:20:21.290
Surveillance! Enemy location?!

01:20:21.290 --> 01:20:23.880
Enemy mobile suits withdrawing!

01:20:32.740 --> 01:20:34.550
If you can't land, don't!

01:20:34.550 --> 01:20:36.510
Secure them with wires!

01:20:38.280 --> 01:20:39.600
Astonaige!

01:20:39.600 --> 01:20:41.060
What?

01:20:42.250 --> 01:20:43.230
Kayra!

01:20:43.230 --> 01:20:44.860
Go to her.

01:20:44.860 --> 01:20:45.770
Right!

01:20:46.670 --> 01:20:48.650
Bring in the next one!

01:20:54.800 --> 01:20:57.120
Astonaige! Stay back!

01:20:57.590 --> 01:20:59.370
Amuro, that's Kayra!

01:20:59.370 --> 01:21:01.330
- Don't look!
- Kayra!

01:21:05.390 --> 01:21:08.090
The funnels were too sensitive.

01:21:08.090 --> 01:21:10.840
They acted quickly
to protect the Gundam...

01:21:10.840 --> 01:21:14.390
I was going to make
your favorite salad.

01:21:14.390 --> 01:21:16.050
Astonaige...

01:21:16.050 --> 01:21:18.310
- Get her out of here!
- Yes, sir!

01:21:20.120 --> 01:21:23.190
It's partly because I couldn't
control the funnels.

01:21:23.190 --> 01:21:25.060
But Char started all this.

01:21:25.060 --> 01:21:27.770
I'm prepared to give my life
to end his.

01:21:27.770 --> 01:21:30.450
Amuro, stop talking like that!

01:21:30.450 --> 01:21:33.110
Now you know how I feel.

01:21:35.590 --> 01:21:37.240
Everywhere, Char...

01:21:44.060 --> 01:21:47.040
So, we won't have any time
to test the Alpha-Azieru?

01:21:47.040 --> 01:21:50.050
Why don't you have Quess
test it in real combat?

01:21:50.050 --> 01:21:52.380
Do you have to sound
so standoffish?

01:21:52.380 --> 01:21:54.260
Did Quess say something to you?

01:21:54.260 --> 01:21:57.800
She told me you're too serious
for her to get along with.

01:21:57.800 --> 01:21:58.970
How's it coming?

01:22:00.240 --> 01:22:04.060
Cruiser 4 will be bringing us
the warheads in 30 minutes.

01:22:04.060 --> 01:22:08.150
Gyunei's frantic that he's
going to lose Quess to you.

01:22:08.620 --> 01:22:11.110
If we send them
forward together...

01:22:11.110 --> 01:22:13.190
...that will bring out his abilities.

01:22:13.190 --> 01:22:14.740
She'll be in the Alpha.

01:22:14.740 --> 01:22:16.910
I can't break a promise.

01:22:16.910 --> 01:22:19.490
I'll abide by
whatever you decide.

01:22:19.490 --> 01:22:21.810
Is that okay?

01:22:21.810 --> 01:22:24.720
If I knew you truly loved me.

01:22:24.720 --> 01:22:27.350
I need you here with me.

01:22:27.350 --> 01:22:28.460
Nanai.

01:22:29.890 --> 01:22:31.500
Char Aznable...

01:22:31.500 --> 01:22:35.260
Are you tired from having to
uphold the Casval Deikun name?

01:22:35.510 --> 01:22:38.890
It hasn't been easy
taking on my father's name.

01:22:39.530 --> 01:22:42.310
I need the support you give me.

01:22:46.160 --> 01:22:47.440
Is that it?

01:22:49.520 --> 01:22:52.150
The Alpha is already completed?

01:22:52.150 --> 01:22:54.690
The Captain told me he's
going to let me use it!

01:22:54.690 --> 01:22:57.030
You've got to be kidding!

01:22:58.160 --> 01:23:00.870
- Everyone's being mean to me!
- That's not true.

01:23:00.870 --> 01:23:02.830
What're you doing?!

01:23:02.830 --> 01:23:05.040
Weren't you with the Captain?

01:23:05.040 --> 01:23:06.370
He's meeting with Nanai.

01:23:06.370 --> 01:23:08.370
Are they just talking business?

01:23:08.370 --> 01:23:09.880
The Captain doesn't care for her.

01:23:09.880 --> 01:23:12.090
He held me in his arms.

01:23:12.090 --> 01:23:14.150
I told you to cool it with him.

01:23:14.150 --> 01:23:15.920
Why should I?

01:23:16.320 --> 01:23:20.740
You know, I wiped out all
of the enemy nukes at once!

01:23:20.740 --> 01:23:23.810
I can get more done
than the Captain himself.

01:23:23.810 --> 01:23:26.060
Forget about that guy!

01:23:26.060 --> 01:23:27.230
What're you saying?!

01:23:27.230 --> 01:23:28.690
There's a war going on!

01:23:28.690 --> 01:23:29.900
Oh, Quess.

01:23:29.900 --> 01:23:33.480
Don't you know why he
keeps Nanai by his side?

01:23:33.480 --> 01:23:36.240
He said he'll see her only on duty.

01:23:37.630 --> 01:23:39.080
I'm fine!

01:23:39.080 --> 01:23:42.580
The Captain's obsessed with
a young pilot named Lalah...

01:23:42.580 --> 01:23:44.830
...who he lost in the
One Year War.

01:23:45.800 --> 01:23:48.460
The reason the Captain
goes out with Nanai...

01:23:48.460 --> 01:23:50.600
...is to keep up appearances
as our leader.

01:23:50.600 --> 01:23:52.840
People think he's into young girls.

01:23:52.840 --> 01:23:55.880
And everyone knows his
true love was Lalah.

01:23:55.880 --> 01:23:57.300
Yeah, so who cares?!

01:23:57.300 --> 01:23:58.670
She's long gone, right?

01:23:58.670 --> 01:24:02.930
Many girls have heard the Captain
mumble Lalah's name in his sleep.

01:24:04.610 --> 01:24:05.600
Quess...

01:24:05.600 --> 01:24:08.270
I'm going to kick Nanai
and Lalah out of his life!

01:24:08.270 --> 01:24:10.270
It was because Lalah
chose Amuro...

01:24:10.270 --> 01:24:12.020
...that he started this war!

01:24:12.230 --> 01:24:16.570
I hate young men because
they say things like that!

01:24:18.400 --> 01:24:21.920
Our remaining fleet will begin
a second attack from this point.

01:24:21.920 --> 01:24:24.240
But those nuclear weapons in Axis...

01:24:24.240 --> 01:24:26.950
...seized from Luna II could still
cause a nuclear winter...

01:24:26.950 --> 01:24:29.330
...if they are detonated
close to Earth.

01:24:29.330 --> 01:24:32.830
So, this time we have
to destroy the thrusters on Axis...

01:24:32.830 --> 01:24:35.460
...and then continue
to destroy Axis itself.

01:24:35.460 --> 01:24:38.960
Which means we have to
carry out an all-out attack.

01:24:38.960 --> 01:24:41.760
The problem is we have
four nukes left.

01:24:41.760 --> 01:24:44.550
If we fail to blast it
with those warheads...

01:24:44.550 --> 01:24:45.930
...we'll have to sneak into Axis...

01:24:45.930 --> 01:24:48.060
...and blow up this section
from the inside.

01:24:48.060 --> 01:24:50.480
There's a network of
mining tunnels...

01:24:50.480 --> 01:24:52.830
...so, it is possible to
break Axis apart.

01:24:52.830 --> 01:24:56.770
Once that happens, the fragments
of Axis will be blown clear of Earth.

01:24:57.210 --> 01:24:59.490
Right. That's a three-stage plan.

01:24:59.490 --> 01:25:03.700
We must complete it before enemy
reinforcements arrive from Luna II.

01:25:06.240 --> 01:25:07.450
Everyone.

01:25:07.450 --> 01:25:09.160
Would you give up your lives?

01:25:16.390 --> 01:25:18.130
"That psyco-frame idea..."

01:25:18.130 --> 01:25:21.130
"It wasn't dreamed up within
our R & D division after all."

01:25:21.130 --> 01:25:23.880
"The R & D people aren't
positive about this, but..."

01:25:23.880 --> 01:25:27.050
"...they think the technology
was provided by Neo Zeon."

01:25:27.050 --> 01:25:29.170
That's ridiculous.

01:25:29.170 --> 01:25:31.840
The psyco-frame worked.

01:25:31.840 --> 01:25:35.150
And the enemy wouldn't
share a finished product.

01:25:35.830 --> 01:25:37.480
Mr. October...

01:25:37.480 --> 01:25:41.030
Why would you send a letter like
this with the psyco-frame sample?

01:25:41.030 --> 01:25:42.530
Chan.

01:25:42.530 --> 01:25:43.360
Yes?!

01:25:43.710 --> 01:25:45.160
What's wrong?

01:25:45.840 --> 01:25:48.120
Thinking of Kayra and Astonaige.

01:25:48.120 --> 01:25:51.740
And you talking about giving
up your life. I'm just worried.

01:25:51.740 --> 01:25:53.330
I apologize.

01:25:53.330 --> 01:25:54.540
The funnels okay?

01:25:54.710 --> 01:25:55.750
Of course.

01:25:55.750 --> 01:25:58.880
I heard that this psyco-frame
can resonate...

01:25:58.880 --> 01:26:01.800
...with your psycommu and
bring unknown powers.

01:26:01.800 --> 01:26:02.880
Do you believe that?

01:26:02.880 --> 01:26:04.780
What October said?

01:26:04.780 --> 01:26:06.840
- I doubt it.
- But...

01:26:07.950 --> 01:26:10.390
I'll win with the Fin Funnels.

01:26:13.530 --> 01:26:16.060
I did create the basic design
of Nu Gundam...

01:26:16.060 --> 01:26:19.020
...and you've been
taking care of it.

01:26:19.330 --> 01:26:21.330
Yeah, I guess you're right!

01:26:21.330 --> 01:26:23.860
Wait right here.
I'll go check and see.

01:26:23.860 --> 01:26:24.780
Okay.

01:26:34.250 --> 01:26:35.790
If we stick around here...

01:26:35.790 --> 01:26:38.130
...we'll be finished when
Hong Kong's hit!

01:26:38.130 --> 01:26:40.380
Is it true another meteor's coming!

01:26:40.380 --> 01:26:43.130
I doubt we'll have
a nuclear winter.

01:26:43.770 --> 01:26:45.940
- Let's take a detour.
- What?

01:26:45.940 --> 01:26:48.280
We'll have to double back, though.

01:26:48.280 --> 01:26:49.970
The sun...

01:26:54.490 --> 01:26:56.890
Mom! What's that?!

01:26:59.460 --> 01:27:02.650
That's Char's asteroid!

01:27:03.540 --> 01:27:05.950
Moving objects likely
the enemy fleet!

01:27:05.950 --> 01:27:08.300
All hands, combat alert 1!

01:27:08.300 --> 01:27:09.660
Are you certain?

01:27:09.660 --> 01:27:11.450
I see Cruiser 4 for sure...

01:27:11.450 --> 01:27:12.620
...but...

01:27:12.620 --> 01:27:15.120
We took this before
scattering Minovsky.

01:27:15.120 --> 01:27:16.910
See the number of lights?

01:27:16.910 --> 01:27:18.960
You're saying they're
Federation fleets?

01:27:18.960 --> 01:27:23.080
From Side 2 and Side 5, and even
those that escaped from Luna II.

01:27:23.080 --> 01:27:25.340
Deploy the mobile suits
to the front!

01:27:25.340 --> 01:27:26.720
Get the Captain!

01:27:32.860 --> 01:27:35.110
Return safely.

01:27:35.110 --> 01:27:38.530
You have permission
from the Captain.

01:27:38.530 --> 01:27:40.810
The combat bridge is off limits.

01:27:40.810 --> 01:27:44.360
But if you can sit still,
you're welcome to observe.

01:27:44.360 --> 01:27:45.110
Y-Yes, sir...!

01:27:45.110 --> 01:27:47.030
Write your will on this.

01:27:47.030 --> 01:27:49.510
- It'll be sent off in a capsule.
- Yes, sir.

01:27:49.510 --> 01:27:52.490
- Add a lock of your hair, too.
- Okay...

01:27:53.630 --> 01:27:55.370
Federation fleets are mobilizing?

01:27:55.370 --> 01:27:56.790
No mistake about it.

01:27:56.790 --> 01:27:59.080
Nu Gundam. Let's do it!

01:27:59.080 --> 01:28:02.130
Ra-Zyme and Ra-Kiem!
You're next!

01:28:03.140 --> 01:28:06.550
They're coming from Side 2 and
Side 5, but will they back us up?

01:28:06.550 --> 01:28:09.760
Inform them of our position
periodically.

01:28:13.110 --> 01:28:17.180
Mobile suit forces to spread out
in advance of the fleet!

01:28:17.560 --> 01:28:19.850
102! You're clear!

01:28:19.850 --> 01:28:21.080
Captain!

01:28:21.080 --> 01:28:22.520
Where did you go?

01:28:22.520 --> 01:28:25.570
Am I a substitute for Lalah?

01:28:25.920 --> 01:28:27.320
Quess...

01:28:28.920 --> 01:28:30.530
Who said that?

01:28:30.530 --> 01:28:32.870
I mean, why would
that bother you?

01:28:32.870 --> 01:28:35.120
I love you! That's why!

01:28:35.120 --> 01:28:36.990
- That's a problem.
- Why?!

01:28:36.990 --> 01:28:40.330
I'd even give up my life for you!

01:28:40.330 --> 01:28:41.330
All right.

01:28:41.330 --> 01:28:44.630
I'll forget about both
Lalah and Nanai.

01:28:46.730 --> 01:28:50.380
Then, I'll protect you with Alpha!

01:28:50.380 --> 01:28:51.510
Char!

01:28:51.510 --> 01:28:56.260
You even wrote something up
for your father. That's good.

01:28:56.700 --> 01:28:57.890
Hathaway.

01:28:59.080 --> 01:29:01.820
Go down below
if you get scared.

01:29:01.820 --> 01:29:03.980
Sure, Dad.

01:29:12.460 --> 01:29:13.160
What's up?

01:29:13.160 --> 01:29:16.120
I had a meeting with
the Operations Officer.

01:29:16.120 --> 01:29:19.700
What made you think
I have an interest in Quess?

01:29:19.700 --> 01:29:21.750
I don't understand, Captain...

01:29:21.750 --> 01:29:24.330
Nanai assigned Quess
to the Alpha.

01:29:24.330 --> 01:29:26.290
Guard her until she gets used to it.

01:29:26.290 --> 01:29:27.590
Yes, sir.

01:29:27.590 --> 01:29:32.090
I'm only interested in Neo Zeon
and defeating Amuro.

01:29:32.480 --> 01:29:34.930
And Nanai's been very nice to me.

01:29:34.930 --> 01:29:36.180
Yes, sir.

01:29:37.150 --> 01:29:39.140
- Gyunei!
- Right!

01:29:41.410 --> 01:29:42.890
Get in!

01:29:45.960 --> 01:29:48.730
I'll soon find out
if he's telling the truth.

01:29:50.570 --> 01:29:53.490
Switch over control
to the combat bridge!

01:29:53.490 --> 01:29:54.410
Thank you.

01:29:54.410 --> 01:29:57.830
You won't have to go out today.

01:29:57.830 --> 01:29:59.620
Let's hope not.

01:29:59.620 --> 01:30:02.080
Quess and the Alpha seem to be
made for each other.

01:30:02.080 --> 01:30:03.470
Is that so?

01:30:03.470 --> 01:30:05.750
Alpha-Azieru, prepare for launch!

01:30:05.750 --> 01:30:07.790
All hands!
Assume combat positions!

01:30:07.790 --> 01:30:09.590
Alpha-Azieru.

01:30:20.160 --> 01:30:21.850
Come on! Come on!

01:30:24.330 --> 01:30:26.020
Don't get carried away, Quess!

01:30:26.270 --> 01:30:28.690
There's a ton of things to do!

01:30:42.720 --> 01:30:44.540
More playful than hostile.

01:30:44.540 --> 01:30:47.460
It's not Char, or that other guy.

01:30:48.040 --> 01:30:49.130
What?

01:30:49.130 --> 01:30:51.500
Someone's blocking my senses.

01:30:54.360 --> 01:30:54.970
Quess!

01:30:54.970 --> 01:30:57.820
That's Nu Gundam!
It's tough!

01:30:57.820 --> 01:30:59.300
Oh, yeah?!

01:31:15.170 --> 01:31:17.570
I don't have time to
play with children.

01:31:17.570 --> 01:31:19.160
What's it doing?

01:31:28.770 --> 01:31:30.790
Get out of here!

01:31:34.060 --> 01:31:35.630
What're those?

01:31:37.510 --> 01:31:39.930
Go down! Go down!

01:31:44.240 --> 01:31:45.270
Quess!

01:31:45.270 --> 01:31:47.350
The Gundam is over here!

01:31:51.000 --> 01:31:53.230
You're out of luck, Gundam!

01:31:55.280 --> 01:31:56.650
Get him!

01:32:06.180 --> 01:32:08.790
Stop playing around
with the small fries!

01:32:08.790 --> 01:32:10.120
Small fries?

01:32:32.900 --> 01:32:35.070
How about this?!

01:32:40.090 --> 01:32:42.280
You're not getting to the Captain!

01:32:42.280 --> 01:32:44.240
Hostile now!

01:32:45.970 --> 01:32:47.660
Oh, no!

01:32:49.930 --> 01:32:51.580
Six enemy units!

01:33:01.940 --> 01:33:04.090
If that's Quess, stop it!

01:33:11.040 --> 01:33:12.640
Gyunei!

01:33:13.270 --> 01:33:14.980
I know!

01:33:14.980 --> 01:33:17.900
Why are his funnels
lasting so long?!

01:33:17.900 --> 01:33:21.280
Stop being such a pain
to the Captain!

01:33:24.760 --> 01:33:26.660
Nu Gundam is alone,
out in front!

01:33:26.830 --> 01:33:28.580
Where are the mobile suit backup?!

01:33:28.580 --> 01:33:30.050
They're doing the best they can!

01:33:30.050 --> 01:33:32.000
You won't get anywhere
being angry at each other!

01:33:32.250 --> 01:33:35.000
Quess!
What you're doing is wrong!

01:33:39.360 --> 01:33:41.800
Chan! What're you doing?!

01:33:41.800 --> 01:33:43.630
There aren't enough
mobile suits out there!

01:33:43.630 --> 01:33:45.400
No, not that one!

01:33:45.400 --> 01:33:47.300
Stop it, Chan!

01:33:47.300 --> 01:33:49.310
But I've repaired one
of the main engines.

01:33:49.310 --> 01:33:51.200
That's not what I...!

01:33:51.200 --> 01:33:52.980
You out of your mind?! Chan!

01:33:52.980 --> 01:33:55.310
Amuro needs more psyco-frames.

01:33:55.560 --> 01:33:57.060
Chan!

01:33:57.060 --> 01:33:59.020
Stop!

01:34:15.080 --> 01:34:17.670
Cruiser 4 has entered Axis.

01:34:17.670 --> 01:34:22.050
Good. Program the warheads to
detonate just before it hits Earth.

01:34:22.400 --> 01:34:23.760
And retrieve the crew.

01:34:23.760 --> 01:34:24.680
Captain.

01:34:24.680 --> 01:34:26.970
I won't stop you now,
but once you beat Amuro...

01:34:27.220 --> 01:34:30.220
Right.
I'll do whatever you ask, then.

01:34:30.220 --> 01:34:32.770
- Now move to the combat bridge.
- Sure.

01:34:34.120 --> 01:34:35.850
Good girl.

01:34:48.420 --> 01:34:51.120
Quess is in that cluster of lights.

01:34:52.390 --> 01:34:54.200
This thing moves!

01:35:10.570 --> 01:35:12.600
Will the funnels last longer?

01:35:12.600 --> 01:35:14.350
No, Quess! Stop it!

01:35:20.110 --> 01:35:21.570
What?

01:35:26.000 --> 01:35:28.280
Did you get Gyunei?!

01:35:31.720 --> 01:35:34.290
They're about to give Axis
its final boost.

01:35:34.290 --> 01:35:35.390
Nuclear missiles!

01:35:35.390 --> 01:35:36.290
They're here!

01:35:36.290 --> 01:35:37.410
Evade!

01:35:43.190 --> 01:35:45.810
Look, Ra-Chutter is
acting as a shield!

01:35:45.810 --> 01:35:47.220
Target the thrusters!

01:35:47.220 --> 01:35:49.260
In a minute, sir!

01:35:51.320 --> 01:35:52.640
Retrieving Cruiser 4 crew!

01:35:52.640 --> 01:35:54.470
And the self-detonators
for the warheads?

01:35:54.470 --> 01:35:55.770
All set, sir!

01:35:55.770 --> 01:35:57.140
Head to the front!

01:35:57.140 --> 01:35:59.600
Prepare Musaka to crush
the Londo-Bell fleet!

01:36:02.160 --> 01:36:04.480
Axis has begun to accelerate!

01:36:04.480 --> 01:36:06.400
Fire missiles toward its rear!

01:36:07.670 --> 01:36:09.840
If the target moves,
lock on again!

01:36:09.840 --> 01:36:12.090
Estimating course! Locked on!

01:36:12.090 --> 01:36:13.910
Good! Fire!

01:36:20.390 --> 01:36:23.090
Which are the nukes?
Funnels!

01:36:25.900 --> 01:36:28.350
They couldn't have that many.

01:36:28.350 --> 01:36:29.550
There!

01:36:34.030 --> 01:36:36.140
They've hit the nuclear missiles?

01:36:36.570 --> 01:36:38.930
Hathaway! Amuro!

01:36:39.830 --> 01:36:41.350
Another one?

01:36:46.000 --> 01:36:48.440
Great move, Bright.
What?

01:36:56.240 --> 01:36:57.410
Ra-Chutter!

01:36:57.410 --> 01:36:59.000
Our missiles have been hit!

01:36:59.000 --> 01:37:00.040
As a shield?!

01:37:00.040 --> 01:37:04.330
We'll land Ra-Cailum on Axis!
Prepare for ground combat!

01:37:04.330 --> 01:37:07.250
All hands, prepare for ground
combat!

01:37:07.250 --> 01:37:08.460
Hathaway?!

01:37:12.360 --> 01:37:13.680
Over here?

01:37:13.680 --> 01:37:15.180
There! Hathaway!

01:37:17.640 --> 01:37:20.770
What's that? Is it Quess?

01:37:23.870 --> 01:37:27.900
The psycommu's guiding me,
so you won't get away!

01:37:29.210 --> 01:37:31.550
Quess! That's you, right?!

01:37:31.550 --> 01:37:33.800
He's being a bit too friendly!

01:37:33.800 --> 01:37:36.120
No! You'll be destroyed!

01:37:37.180 --> 01:37:39.160
Oh, no! She's...!

01:37:40.620 --> 01:37:42.040
What the?!

01:37:42.680 --> 01:37:44.870
Move, Hathaway!

01:37:45.180 --> 01:37:46.580
That thing...!

01:37:49.500 --> 01:37:51.090
Stop it, Quess!

01:37:51.090 --> 01:37:53.430
That's why you're always
making enemies, Quess!

01:37:53.430 --> 01:37:55.390
You creepy Earthnoids!

01:37:55.390 --> 01:38:00.070
I have to destroy that planet,
or we won't be saved!

01:38:00.070 --> 01:38:01.330
What?

01:38:01.330 --> 01:38:03.520
Quess! I can tell you're there!

01:38:03.770 --> 01:38:05.100
Open the hatch!

01:38:05.100 --> 01:38:07.940
Once you see my face,
you'll forget your anger.

01:38:08.110 --> 01:38:11.070
I hate children!
They're so annoying!

01:38:13.360 --> 01:38:15.280
Hathaway! Get out of there!

01:38:15.280 --> 01:38:17.160
That girl's dangerous!

01:38:18.010 --> 01:38:19.280
You disgusting woman.

01:38:19.280 --> 01:38:22.580
I could've stayed with Amuro
if only you weren't around!

01:38:22.580 --> 01:38:24.540
Stayed with Amuro?

01:38:24.540 --> 01:38:25.830
Does she?!

01:38:25.830 --> 01:38:27.040
Quess! Get out!

01:38:27.290 --> 01:38:28.670
Hathaway!

01:38:30.310 --> 01:38:33.800
It'll hit...!
Get back, Hathaway!

01:38:35.860 --> 01:38:37.090
Quess!

01:38:40.010 --> 01:38:42.020
Quess!

01:38:47.290 --> 01:38:48.980
Hathaway, are you okay?!

01:38:48.980 --> 01:38:52.150
Chan?! You did that?!

01:38:54.040 --> 01:38:54.990
Stop it.

01:38:54.990 --> 01:38:56.490
Can't you see what?

01:38:56.490 --> 01:38:58.240
You shouldn't have done that!

01:38:58.240 --> 01:39:02.700
You grownups don't understand.
That's why you'll destroy Earth!

01:39:03.510 --> 01:39:05.160
Hathaway!

01:39:24.240 --> 01:39:27.230
Hey. Doesn't Londo-Bell
need some support?

01:39:27.230 --> 01:39:29.270
The battle's already started, right?

01:39:29.270 --> 01:39:30.690
Launch with sleds.

01:39:30.690 --> 01:39:34.190
Never mind how you'll get back.
Just help Londo-Bell.

01:39:34.190 --> 01:39:37.240
Follow me.
Our destination is Axis!

01:39:37.240 --> 01:39:40.380
Head to Axis at maximum speed.
On the double!

01:39:40.380 --> 01:39:42.410
Are they going to pick us up later?

01:39:42.410 --> 01:39:44.240
Just go!

01:39:48.960 --> 01:39:51.840
If we could fly, we'd be in space.

01:39:51.840 --> 01:39:54.090
Should we try?

01:39:57.070 --> 01:39:58.970
The sun...

01:40:00.860 --> 01:40:04.580
Hey. You can see the sun
for a change.

01:40:04.580 --> 01:40:06.450
Christina...!

01:40:06.450 --> 01:40:08.640
Hey.
Did you guys hear something?

01:40:08.640 --> 01:40:10.270
No.

01:40:15.790 --> 01:40:18.150
Skipper! Londo-Bell's coming!
Move out!

01:40:18.400 --> 01:40:20.200
We descend, then advance!

01:40:20.200 --> 01:40:22.370
Mobile suits closing in!

01:40:31.580 --> 01:40:34.590
What're the other ships doing?
Call for back up!

01:40:34.590 --> 01:40:37.460
All channels are cut!

01:40:38.270 --> 01:40:40.760
Geara-Doga team! Return!

01:40:52.330 --> 01:40:54.190
He's here!

01:40:55.900 --> 01:40:58.070
He dodged it! Char!

01:41:01.550 --> 01:41:04.740
I'm not letting you
closer to the thrusters!

01:41:17.380 --> 01:41:19.340
He dodged that, too!

01:41:21.730 --> 01:41:24.300
You're a worthy opponent!

01:41:25.700 --> 01:41:27.600
A cruiser?!

01:41:32.740 --> 01:41:34.600
Why is it here?

01:41:34.600 --> 01:41:36.820
Of course! Char!

01:41:39.730 --> 01:41:41.440
Amuro! Not so fast!

01:41:41.440 --> 01:41:43.610
Funnels!

01:41:44.420 --> 01:41:45.700
Char!

01:41:53.560 --> 01:41:57.170
I can't contaminate the Earth
if they blow up here!

01:42:02.020 --> 01:42:05.090
Amuro! Don't you realize
the humans remaining on Earth...

01:42:05.090 --> 01:42:08.760
...they're just vermin
infesting the planet?!

01:42:15.290 --> 01:42:16.310
It's been hit!

01:42:16.310 --> 01:42:19.570
Cruiser 4's warheads
have detonated!

01:42:23.040 --> 01:42:26.990
What's this force?
Ra-Cailum! Give me details!

01:42:26.990 --> 01:42:29.780
There's a huge flash
of light in front!

01:42:29.780 --> 01:42:31.490
Its cause... is unknown!

01:42:31.800 --> 01:42:33.600
Wire's broken!

01:42:33.600 --> 01:42:36.170
Speed up the blasting operations!

01:42:36.170 --> 01:42:37.710
Where's the Gundam now?

01:42:37.710 --> 01:42:40.170
Ra-Cailum has landed?!

01:42:41.560 --> 01:42:43.210
A thruster's gone?!

01:42:43.210 --> 01:42:45.930
Amuro! You won't get any more!

01:42:46.690 --> 01:42:49.100
Above our bow! Counter!

01:43:04.590 --> 01:43:05.990
Chan?!

01:43:06.460 --> 01:43:08.110
Is he coming?!

01:43:10.990 --> 01:43:12.660
Amuro...

01:43:21.290 --> 01:43:25.340
Remember the pain you suffered
when you killed Lalah!

01:43:40.460 --> 01:43:41.560
You're pathetic!

01:43:41.560 --> 01:43:42.690
Me?!

01:43:44.380 --> 01:43:49.200
Why won't you realize that you're
wasting your precious talents?!

01:43:51.170 --> 01:43:52.700
Same to you!

01:43:57.410 --> 01:43:59.420
What, I've lost power?!

01:44:00.520 --> 01:44:01.960
You're taking too long!

01:44:01.960 --> 01:44:03.870
We're almost done.

01:44:03.870 --> 01:44:06.550
This'll blow Axis to pieces.

01:44:27.920 --> 01:44:30.200
Ra-Cailum's here!

01:44:30.200 --> 01:44:31.740
What?!

01:44:33.620 --> 01:44:37.950
Blow up Axis from inside even if
it means sacrificing the Gundam?!

01:44:37.950 --> 01:44:39.620
I won't let that happen!

01:44:50.690 --> 01:44:54.550
I guess Bright's team
haven't come up yet.

01:45:12.670 --> 01:45:14.030
He got away!

01:45:15.680 --> 01:45:18.450
There are some things
you don't understand.

01:45:18.450 --> 01:45:20.540
Revolutions are dreamt up
by intellectuals...

01:45:20.750 --> 01:45:24.960
...but reality forces them
to take drastic measures.

01:45:25.270 --> 01:45:27.750
Where are the radio
signals coming from?

01:45:27.750 --> 01:45:29.510
Following a revolution...

01:45:29.510 --> 01:45:33.890
...the passions for a rebirth get
taken over by mediocrity.

01:45:34.140 --> 01:45:35.680
Intellectuals hate this...

01:45:35.680 --> 01:45:38.890
...and withdraw from society
and politics to become recluses.

01:45:38.890 --> 01:45:39.680
Eventually...

01:45:39.680 --> 01:45:42.980
I'm not planning to
change the world!

01:45:55.420 --> 01:45:59.260
Those ignorant people are just
taking advantage of your powers!

01:45:59.260 --> 01:46:00.540
Think so?!

01:46:18.030 --> 01:46:21.310
He escaped?
And Bright's team, too?

01:46:50.150 --> 01:46:51.880
That was nothing!

01:46:54.730 --> 01:46:57.470
My saber's weaker than his?

01:46:59.150 --> 01:47:00.560
What the?!

01:47:03.100 --> 01:47:04.430
Char!

01:47:07.400 --> 01:47:09.900
If it hadn't been for you...!

01:47:13.920 --> 01:47:15.490
Amuro!

01:47:19.170 --> 01:47:20.990
My monitor's failing!

01:47:20.990 --> 01:47:22.240
What?!

01:47:23.370 --> 01:47:25.120
Sink the Rewloola!

01:47:25.120 --> 01:47:27.250
We're barely hanging
on ourselves!

01:47:27.250 --> 01:47:28.500
We've got to withdraw!

01:47:28.500 --> 01:47:30.380
Do you want to go down
with Axis?!

01:47:30.380 --> 01:47:31.840
- It's time!
- Uh-oh.

01:47:38.680 --> 01:47:40.510
They pulled it off?!

01:47:44.370 --> 01:47:46.350
What's that? I'm to retreat?

01:47:46.350 --> 01:47:47.230
Nanai!

01:47:47.230 --> 01:47:49.940
Don't interfere in a battle
between men!

01:47:53.880 --> 01:47:55.360
Captain!

01:47:55.360 --> 01:47:58.610
We still need you.
Don't abandon us!

01:47:58.610 --> 01:48:01.410
Surveillance team, heads up!

01:48:02.700 --> 01:48:04.950
You're not going anywhere!

01:48:09.420 --> 01:48:13.170
He caught me.
But it's too late!

01:48:15.880 --> 01:48:18.760
- Pursue the Rewloola!
- Incoming fragments!

01:48:18.760 --> 01:48:19.840
Mobile suit team!

01:48:19.840 --> 01:48:21.680
- Is it true, Meran?
- Yes, sir!

01:48:21.680 --> 01:48:23.760
The front piece will clear Earth.

01:48:23.760 --> 01:48:27.310
But the explosion
braked the rear piece!

01:48:27.310 --> 01:48:29.020
It should stay in orbit, though!

01:48:29.020 --> 01:48:33.060
But the explosion
had too much force!

01:48:33.370 --> 01:48:36.190
So, we assisted Char?

01:48:37.000 --> 01:48:39.950
D-Dad... Dad!

01:48:47.300 --> 01:48:49.580
What are you laughing about?!

01:48:49.580 --> 01:48:51.420
Looks like I win.

01:48:51.420 --> 01:48:52.790
According to my calculation...

01:48:52.790 --> 01:48:56.000
...the back end of Axis is being
pulled in by Earth's gravity.

01:48:56.000 --> 01:48:57.800
Your plan has backfired!

01:48:57.800 --> 01:48:59.050
So you think!

01:48:59.050 --> 01:49:03.300
I'll use the Gundam to push back
that worthless piece of rock!

01:49:05.410 --> 01:49:06.930
Don't be stupid!

01:49:06.930 --> 01:49:08.640
I'll just have to try!

01:49:08.640 --> 01:49:09.600
You're insane!

01:49:09.770 --> 01:49:12.100
I'm not as impatient as you!

01:49:12.100 --> 01:49:15.360
I can wait for humanity
to learn and grow!

01:49:17.960 --> 01:49:20.650
Axis is starting to
free fall to Earth!

01:49:20.650 --> 01:49:23.280
You're underestimating
Nu Gundam!

01:49:33.890 --> 01:49:35.920
Use the Ra-Cailum
to push back Axis!

01:49:35.920 --> 01:49:37.130
That's crazy!

01:49:37.130 --> 01:49:39.590
Are you going to sit and
watch the Earth be ruined!

01:49:39.590 --> 01:49:42.970
But the Rewloola hasn't
been destroyed yet!

01:49:45.490 --> 01:49:48.180
Captain. Tell me you won't...

01:49:50.700 --> 01:49:53.230
Axis is accelerating!

01:49:53.230 --> 01:49:55.350
Check our mobile suit unit!

01:49:55.350 --> 01:49:56.190
Sir!

01:49:56.960 --> 01:50:01.110
Amuro, are you still at Axis?

01:50:06.760 --> 01:50:08.280
If I feared for my life...

01:50:08.280 --> 01:50:12.080
...I would never have dared
to give you the psyco-frame data!

01:50:12.080 --> 01:50:13.000
What?

01:50:13.000 --> 01:50:17.540
It would be my hollow victory if
you had a second-rate mobile suit.

01:50:17.540 --> 01:50:19.750
But this has become absurd!

01:50:19.960 --> 01:50:21.420
You're so arrogant.

01:50:21.420 --> 01:50:25.800
Why do you always have to
look down on other people?

01:50:34.700 --> 01:50:36.310
- What?!
- Heat source!

01:50:36.310 --> 01:50:39.230
Axis is burning up!

01:50:41.960 --> 01:50:43.590
Captain...

01:50:43.590 --> 01:50:45.400
What's wrong, Nanai?

01:50:45.400 --> 01:50:48.490
The Captain's life
is draining away.

01:50:48.490 --> 01:50:50.540
Enemy reinforcements confirmed!

01:50:50.540 --> 01:50:53.580
Feddie mobile suits approaching
from the far side of the Earth!

01:50:53.580 --> 01:50:56.290
You sure it's not just
a computer simulation decoy?

01:50:56.290 --> 01:50:57.460
It's a live image!

01:50:57.460 --> 01:50:59.290
How many are there?!

01:50:59.290 --> 01:51:00.960
From the far side of Earth?!

01:51:00.960 --> 01:51:03.090
They're not allies!

01:51:04.820 --> 01:51:06.680
From the portside, too!

01:51:06.680 --> 01:51:08.590
From the Earth Federation Forces?

01:51:08.590 --> 01:51:10.100
I'm positive, sir!

01:51:11.410 --> 01:51:12.890
From the 88th fleet!

01:51:12.890 --> 01:51:14.200
But why?

01:51:14.200 --> 01:51:17.690
And they're all headed
toward Axis.

01:51:21.420 --> 01:51:24.900
"Ra-Cailum requested to retrieve
damaged units." End message.

01:51:24.900 --> 01:51:28.950
Why now?
Why are they joining in?

01:51:29.550 --> 01:51:31.490
Could that light from Axis...

01:51:31.490 --> 01:51:35.620
...be caused by the psyco-frame
that Chan mentioned?

01:51:37.810 --> 01:51:40.250
What are they trying to do?

01:51:45.190 --> 01:51:47.510
What?
What are you doing?

01:52:00.560 --> 01:52:01.940
Stop it!

01:52:01.940 --> 01:52:03.610
You don't have to do this!

01:52:03.770 --> 01:52:05.900
Stay back! Don't come!

01:52:05.900 --> 01:52:08.950
What is it? What's going on here?

01:52:09.550 --> 01:52:12.740
I was sure my plan was flawless!

01:52:13.280 --> 01:52:15.790
We won't let Londo-Bell
take all the credit!

01:52:15.790 --> 01:52:18.960
But your suits won't hold!

01:52:32.150 --> 01:52:33.970
Geara-Dogas, too?!

01:52:33.970 --> 01:52:36.100
It's no use! Get back!

01:52:36.100 --> 01:52:38.640
Earth's fate rests in the balance!

01:52:38.640 --> 01:52:39.850
It's worth a try!

01:52:39.850 --> 01:52:43.650
But some of the suits are exploding!

01:52:46.670 --> 01:52:47.900
No!

01:52:47.900 --> 01:52:52.240
You'll just destroy yourselves
from the heat and overload!

01:53:01.350 --> 01:53:04.090
Don't do this!
Get out of here!

01:53:04.090 --> 01:53:08.420
In the end, only such sorrow
will spread across until...

01:53:08.420 --> 01:53:10.940
...it finally destroys the Earth.

01:53:10.940 --> 01:53:13.930
Then humans will be forced to
judge themselves by themselves...

01:53:13.930 --> 01:53:18.790
...and they will have to atone for
their sins against nature and Earth.

01:53:18.790 --> 01:53:21.940
Amuro.
Why don't you realize this?

01:53:21.940 --> 01:53:23.910
Get out of here!

01:53:23.910 --> 01:53:26.110
The Gundam's power will...!

01:53:43.430 --> 01:53:46.770
The psyco-frames
must be resonating.

01:53:46.770 --> 01:53:49.050
Human wills concentrated here...

01:53:49.050 --> 01:53:51.340
...have caused an overload?

01:53:51.340 --> 01:53:54.760
But, I sense no fear.

01:53:55.280 --> 01:53:57.720
Rather, I feel warmth.

01:53:58.820 --> 01:54:01.110
I even feel comfort.

01:54:01.110 --> 01:54:03.270
I couldn't do it...

01:54:13.380 --> 01:54:14.950
Behind that curtain of light!

01:54:14.950 --> 01:54:17.160
Mobile suits are
being tossed around!

01:54:17.160 --> 01:54:19.030
We need better surveillance!

01:54:19.030 --> 01:54:21.000
What's happening down there?

01:54:24.680 --> 01:54:26.080
I see.

01:54:26.080 --> 01:54:30.340
Humans, who can possess
warmth, are still cruel
enough to destroy Earth.

01:54:30.690 --> 01:54:32.760
You must understand that, Amuro!

01:54:32.760 --> 01:54:33.970
I do know that.

01:54:33.970 --> 01:54:38.940
That's why we have to show the
world the light of the human heart!

01:54:38.940 --> 01:54:42.520
For a man who thinks that way,
you were awfully cold to Quess.

01:54:42.770 --> 01:54:44.520
I'm not a machine!

01:54:44.520 --> 01:54:47.310
I couldn't be a father figure
to Quess!

01:54:47.310 --> 01:54:48.770
Is that it?

01:54:48.770 --> 01:54:51.360
Is that why you used Quess
like some kind of machine?

01:54:51.360 --> 01:54:55.320
So, Quess was searching
for a father figure.

01:54:55.320 --> 01:54:58.530
I see why I found her annoying...

01:54:58.530 --> 01:55:00.580
...and turned her into a machine.

01:55:00.580 --> 01:55:03.910
I thought you were
more broadminded!

01:55:04.600 --> 01:55:09.310
Lalah Sune was a woman who may
have become a mother to me.

01:55:09.310 --> 01:55:12.250
You took her life,
so don't you judge me!

01:55:12.250 --> 01:55:14.920
Lalah? A mother?

01:55:22.660 --> 01:55:24.100
Captain!

01:55:24.100 --> 01:55:25.640
Hey! Nanai!

01:55:25.640 --> 01:55:26.770
What's the matter?

01:55:26.770 --> 01:55:28.940
Axis is now moving
away from Earth!

01:55:28.940 --> 01:55:30.730
That can't be!

01:55:39.840 --> 01:55:42.280
Axis is definitely changing course!

01:55:42.280 --> 01:55:44.330
It's veering away from Earth!

01:57:41.120 --> 01:57:42.740
YOU BELONG TO ME

01:57:42.740 --> 01:57:45.530
Sayanara ienakute

01:57:42.740 --> 01:57:45.530
I can't say goodbye

01:57:45.530 --> 01:57:50.000
Itsumade mo dakishimeta katta

01:57:45.530 --> 01:57:50.000
I held you forever

01:57:50.000 --> 01:57:51.870
I BELONG TO YOU

01:57:51.870 --> 01:57:54.420
Harisake sou ni naru

01:57:51.870 --> 01:57:54.420
It's ready to burst

01:57:54.420 --> 01:57:58.920
Kono mune o kimi ni sashidashite

01:57:54.420 --> 01:57:58.920
This chest is reaching out for you

01:57:58.920 --> 01:58:00.920
We belong to Earth

01:58:00.920 --> 01:58:03.340
Haruka na sora no moto

01:58:00.920 --> 01:58:03.340
The source of a far away universe

01:58:03.340 --> 01:58:07.850
Kobaruto ni hikaru hoshi ga aru

01:58:03.340 --> 01:58:07.850
Toward the cobalt, there is a shining Earth

01:58:07.850 --> 01:58:12.310
Kanashimi wa soko kara hajimatte

01:58:07.850 --> 01:58:12.310
That is where sadness begins

01:58:12.310 --> 01:58:18.190
Itoshisa ga soko ni kaeru no sa

01:58:12.310 --> 01:58:18.190
All that we love is returning there

01:58:18.400 --> 01:58:27.370
Mebiusu no wakara nukedase nakute

01:58:18.400 --> 01:58:27.370
You can't slip away from the moebius ring

01:58:27.370 --> 01:58:34.290
Ikutsu mono tsumi o kurikaesu

01:58:27.370 --> 01:58:34.290
So many mistakes are repeated

01:58:34.290 --> 01:58:38.790
Heiwa yori jiyuu yori tadashisa yori

01:58:34.290 --> 01:58:38.790
More than peace, more than freedom, more than justice

01:58:38.790 --> 01:58:43.130
Kimi dake ga nozomu subete dakara

01:58:38.790 --> 01:58:43.130
I want you, because you're everything

01:58:43.130 --> 01:58:47.390
Hanarete mo kawatte mo mi ushinatte mo

01:58:43.130 --> 01:58:47.390
